90f29531-c08a-4554-a793-6d076cf2b61b	Alternate arm leg plank	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Start in a plank position with your hands directly under your shoulders and your body forming a straight line from head to heels.\r\n2. Lift your right arm and left leg simultaneously, extending them straight out while maintaining balance. Hold briefly, then lower back to the plank position.\r\n3. Lift your left arm and right leg simultaneously, extending them straight out and holding briefly before returning to the plank position.\r\n4. Continue alternating sides, lifting opposite arms and legs.	1. Keep your core engaged throughout the exercise to maintain stability and prevent your hips from sagging.\r\n2. Perform the movement slowly and with control to maximize muscle engagement and maintain balance.\r\n3. Breathe steadily, exhaling as you lift your arm and leg and inhaling as you lower them back to the plank position.	{"video_url": "videos/Abdominals/Alternate Arm Leg Plank.mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Abdominals/Alternate Arm Leg Plank.jpeg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
