907c4405-b1a7-4bdf-a8c9-35abe21ef29e	Back stretch standing with bench	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Stand tall near an incline bench with your back straight and feet shoulder-width apart.\r\n2. Extend your arms and reach the bench by leaning forward.\r\n3. Hold the bench and extend your back while lowering your chest towards the floor.\r\n4. Hold this position for 15-30 seconds, feeling the stretch in your back.	1. Engage your core muscles to maintain stability and support your lower back during the stretch.\r\n2. Keep your shoulders relaxed and down away from your ears to prevent tension.\r\n3. Make sure your feet are firmly planted on the floor to provide a stable base and enhance the stretch.	{"video_url": "videos/Stretching - Mobility/back stretch standing with bench.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Stretching - Mobility/back stretch standing with bench1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Stretching - Mobility/back stretch standing with bench.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
bd99afd0-9116-4945-a24f-39c8d158e3b5	Backhand Raise	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart, knees bent and lean forward at the hips until your torso is halfway parallel to the floor. Keep your back straight.\r\n2. Extend your arms straight back parallel to your torso with your palms facing backwards.\r\n3. Raise your arms upwards, keeping them straight, until they are over your back.\r\n4. Lower your arms back to the starting position in a controlled manner.	1. Engage your core to maintain stability and support your lower back throughout the exercise.\r\n2. Keep your movements slow and controlled to maximize muscle activation and prevent injury.\r\n3. Focus on squeezing your shoulder blades together at the top of the movement to enhance upper back activation.	{"video_url": "videos/Shoulders/Backhand raise.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Shoulders/Backhand raise1.jpg", "image_female_end": "images/Shoulders/Backhand Raise_female1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Shoulders/Backhand raise.jpg", "image_female_start": "images/Shoulders/Backhand Raise_female.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
30815e34-30be-4372-aaaa-a6c022f75797	Backward abdominal stretch	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Get down on your knees with your back straight, thighs extended, and legs resting on the floor.\r\n2. Lean backward and hold your feet by extending your arms to stretch your abdominal muscles.\r\n3. Maintain this stretch for 30-60 seconds.\r\n	1. Keep your hips stable to ensure a deep and effective stretch.\r\n2. Avoid overextending your back; only lean as far back as is comfortable and safe for your flexibility.\r\n3. Breathe deeply and steadily to help relax your muscles and enhance the stretch.	{"video_url": "videos/Stretching - Mobility/Backward abdominal stretch.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Stretching - Mobility/Backward abdominal stretch1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Stretching - Mobility/Backward abdominal stretch.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
13d760bf-0cae-415b-9354-7256de31d1fe	Backward Forward Turn to Side Neck Stretch	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart and your head in a neutral position.\r\n2. Tilt your head backward, stretching the front of your neck.\r\n3. Return to the neutral position, then tilt your head forward to stretch the back of your neck.\r\n4. Turn your head to one side, holding briefly, and then return to the neutral position. Repeat on the other side.\r\n	1. Perform the movements slowly and gently to avoid straining your neck muscles.\r\n2. Keep your shoulders relaxed and down to prevent tension in your upper back and shoulders.\r\n3. Breathe deeply and steadily to help relax your muscles and enhance the stretch.	{"video_url": "videos/Stretching - Mobility/Backward Forward Turn to Side Neck Stretch.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Stretching - Mobility/Backward Forward Turn to Side Neck Stretch1.jpg", "image_female_end": "images/Stretching - Mobility/Backward Forward Turn to Side Neck Stretch_female1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Stretching - Mobility/Backward Forward Turn to Side Neck Stretch.jpg", "image_female_start": "images/Stretching - Mobility/Backward Forward Turn to Side Neck Stretch_female.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
cda324a7-8a39-4c47-83e7-69c97424aa3b	Balance Board (VERSION 2)	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	9ce42536-8425-4171-a8e2-7f720ad5e136	1. Stand on the balance board with your feet shoulder-width apart.\r\n2. Shift your weight side to side by straightening one leg while lightly bending the other.\r\n3. Shift your weight to the opposite side by bending the extended leg lightly and straightening the other leg.\r\n4. Continue the movement in a controlled, rhythmic manner to improve balance.	1. Focus on a point in front of you to help maintain your balance.\r\n2. Start with slow movements and gradually increase the speed as you become more comfortable.\r\n3. Keep your movements controlled to maximize muscle activation and prevent injury.	{"image_female_end": "images/Legs/Balance Board (VERSION 2)_female1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Legs/Balance Board (VERSION 2)_female.jpg", "image_female_start": "images/Legs/Balance Board (VERSION 2)_female.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
