089c2b12-ed9e-453b-9168-24371872a416	Balloon Drill	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	4b3ab084-5450-45b1-9dbf-057e78d84390	1. Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart, holding a balloon in front of you.\r\n2. Toss the balloon into the air and tap it lightly to keep it afloat.\r\n3. As the balloon is in the air, perform a squat by bending your knees and lowering your hips until your thighs are parallel to the floor.\r\n4. Stand back up and tap the balloon again as it comes down, repeating the process.	1. Start with a shallow squat if you are new to the exercise and gradually increase the depth as you become more comfortable.\r\n2. Focus on keeping your back straight and your knees aligned with your toes during the squat.\r\n3. Perform the movement smoothly and with control to maximize muscle activation and coordination.	{"image_female_end": "images/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Balloon Drill_female1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Balloon Drill_female.jpg", "image_female_start": "images/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Balloon Drill_female.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
