10866f28-d58f-497b-87cb-c1bb00e37b7c	Barbell clean and jerk split squat	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	68ed06e5-fd1e-4198-8eea-6b4b13e3ede2	1. Lean with your feet shoulder-width apart, holding a barbell with an overhand grip. Clean the barbell to your shoulders by explosively lifting it from the floor, shrugging your shoulders, and rotating your wrists so the bar rests on your shoulders with your elbows pointing forward.\r\n2. Engage your core and slightly dip your knees. Explosively push the barbell overhead by extending your legs and arms fully.\r\n3. Step into a split squat position by moving one leg forward and the other leg back, lowering your body until your back knee nearly touches the floor. Ensure your front knee tracks over your toes and your back knee is bent.\r\n4. Push through the heel of your front foot to stand back up, bringing your feet together while keeping the barbell overhead. Carefully lower the barbell back to the starting position. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions, alternating the leg that steps forward for each rep.\r\n	1. Move explosively but with control to ensure proper form and maximize muscle engagement.\r\n2. Ensure your knees track over your toes to prevent knee injuries and maintain proper alignment.\r\n3. Keep your chest up and back straight throughout the movement to maintain proper posture.\r\n	{"video_url": "videos/Powerlifting/Barbell clean and jerk split squat.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Powerlifting/Barbell clean and jerk split squat1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Powerlifting/Barbell clean and jerk split squat.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
bcd4f7f7-c1ce-440a-aa15-593682417c66	Barbell clean and press	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	68ed06e5-fd1e-4198-8eea-6b4b13e3ede2	1. Start in a squatted position with your feet shoulder-width apart, holding a barbell with an overhand grip. The barbell should be on the floor in front of you.\r\n2. Explosively lift the barbell by extending your hips and knees, shrugging your shoulders, and rotating your wrists so the bar rests on your shoulders with your elbows pointing forward (clean position).\r\n3. From the clean position, engage your core and press the barbell overhead by extending your arms fully. Keep the bar slightly behind your head at the top of the movement.\r\n4. Slowly lower the barbell back to your shoulders with control, then return the barbell to the floor by reversing the clean movement. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Focus on leg drive during the clean to generate power from your lower body.\r\n2. Keep your grip firm but not too tight to allow smooth wrist rotation during the clean.\r\n3. Exhale powerfully as you press the bar overhead to stabilize your core.	{"video_url": "videos/Powerlifting/Barbell clean and press.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Powerlifting/Barbell clean and press1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Powerlifting/Barbell clean and press.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
