a34353ff-5df9-4b3c-923b-6b1f02f33bff	Barbell muscle clean	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	68ed06e5-fd1e-4198-8eea-6b4b13e3ede2	1. Begin in a squatted position with your feet hip-width apart, holding a barbell with an overhand grip (palms facing your body), hands slightly wider than shoulder-width apart. The barbell should be resting on the floor.\r\n2. Explosively extend your hips and knees while pulling the barbell up towards your chest, keeping it close to your body. As the barbell passes your knees, shrug your shoulders and continue to pull the barbell upward.\r\n3. Quickly rotate your elbows under the bar and catch it in a front rack position with your elbows pointing forward. Stand up straight to complete the lift.\r\n4. Lower the barbell back to the starting position with control. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Keep the barbell close to your body to ensure an efficient and powerful lift.\r\n2. Focus on an explosive hip extension to generate the necessary force for the clean.\r\n3. Engage your shoulders and traps during the shrug to assist in lifting the barbell.\r\n4. Use your legs and hips rather than relying solely on your arms to lift the barbell.	{"video_url": "videos/Powerlifting/Barbell muscle clean.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Powerlifting/Barbell muscle clean1.jpg", "image_female_end": "images/Powerlifting/barbell muscle clean_female1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Powerlifting/Barbell muscle clean.jpg", "image_female_start": "images/Powerlifting/barbell muscle clean_female.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
