4a725c5e-52c9-4a29-8cae-b639f9b4d232	Barbell wide shrug	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	68ed06e5-fd1e-4198-8eea-6b4b13e3ede2	1. Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart, holding a barbell with an overhand grip (palms facing down), hands placed wider than shoulder-width apart. Allow the barbell to rest against your thighs with your arms fully extended.\r\n2. Raise your shoulders towards your ears as high as possible, keeping your arms straight and the barbell close to your body.\r\n3. Hold the contraction at the top for a moment, squeezing your shoulder blades together.\r\n4. Slowly lower your shoulders back to the starting position. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Keep your arms straight and avoid using your biceps to lift the barbell.\r\n2. Focus on using your trapezius muscles to lift your shoulders, not your arms.\r\n3. Breathe steadily, exhaling as you lift your shoulders and inhaling as you lower them back down.	{"video_url": "videos/Shoulders/Barbell Wide Shrug.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Shoulders/Barbell Wide Shrug1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Shoulders/Barbell Wide Shrug.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
d0b855c2-2c17-430c-9fb2-170913f6c531	Barbell wrist curl on knees	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	68ed06e5-fd1e-4198-8eea-6b4b13e3ede2	1. Sit on a bench with your feet flat on the floor, holding a barbell with an underhand grip (palms facing up), hands placed shoulder-width apart. Rest your forearms on your thighs, allowing your wrists to hang over the edge.\r\n2. Start with your wrists extended so the barbell is lowered as much as possible while maintaining control.\r\n3. Curl the barbell upward by flexing your wrists, lifting the barbell as high as possible while keeping your forearms stationary on your thighs.\r\n4. Slowly lower the barbell back to the starting position by extending your wrists. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Keep your forearms stationary on your thighs to isolate your wrist flexors.\r\n2. Avoid using your elbows to lift the barbell; focus on your wrist movement.\r\n3. Breathe steadily, exhaling as you curl the barbell up and inhaling as you lower it back down.	{"video_url": "videos/Forearms/barbell wrist curl on knees.mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Forearms/barbell wrist curl on knees.jpeg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
8da5b0ae-748b-433d-9d4d-31dec49b1be5	Barbell wrist curl wide legs	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	68ed06e5-fd1e-4198-8eea-6b4b13e3ede2	1. Sit on a bench with your feet spread wide apart, holding a barbell with an underhand grip (palms facing up), hands placed shoulder-width apart. Rest your forearms on the edge of the bench, allowing your wrists to hang over the edge.\r\n2. Start with your wrists extended so the barbell is lowered as much as possible.\r\n3. Curl the barbell upward by flexing your wrists, lifting the barbell as high as possible while keeping your forearms stationary on your thighs.\r\n4. Slowly lower the barbell back to the starting position by extending your wrists. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Keep your forearms stationary on your thighs to isolate your wrist flexors.\r\n2. Avoid using your elbows to lift the barbell; focus on your wrist movement.\r\n3. Breathe steadily, exhaling as you curl the barbell up and inhaling as you lower it back down.	{"video_url": "videos/Forearms/barbell wrist curl wide legs.mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Forearms/barbell wrist curl wide legs.jpeg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
