0c7a762b-3d7f-4869-9616-44053a9f8b60	Bench dip (knees bent)	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Sit on the edge of a bench with your hands placed on the bench beside your hips.\r\n2. Slide your hips off the bench, supporting your body with your hands, and bend your knees at a 90-degree angle with your feet flat on the floor.\r\n3. Lower your body by bending your elbows until your upper arms are parallel to the floor.\r\n4. Push through your palms to raise your body back to the starting position.	1. Keep your elbows pointed backward and close to your body to engage your triceps effectively.\r\n2. Avoid locking your elbows at the top of the movement to maintain tension in your triceps.\r\n3. Perform the movement slowly and with control to maximize muscle activation and prevent injury.	{"video_url": "videos/Triceps/Bench Dip (knees bent).mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Triceps/Bench Dip (knees bent).jpeg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
