df2cf3eb-3e79-4e99-a20a-ac2ba3ef4b96	Calf stretch with hands against wall	Resistance	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	de08e8c8-a4ec-465b-ae07-cc976f64cd81	1. Stand facing a wall with your feet shoulder-width apart. Place your hands on the wall at shoulder height and shoulder-width apart.\r\n2. Step one foot back, keeping your back leg straight and your front leg slightly bent. Press your back heel into the floor.\r\n3. Lean forward slightly, pushing against the wall to deepen the stretch in your calf.\r\n4. Hold the stretch for 20-30 seconds, then switch legs and repeat.	1. Keep your back leg straight and your heel pressed into the floor to maximize the stretch.\r\n2. Stretch both legs equally to maintain balanced flexibility.\r\n3. Breathe deeply and steadily throughout the stretch to help relax your muscles.	{"video_url": "videos/Stretching - Mobility/Calf Stretch With Hands Against Wall.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Stretching - Mobility/Calf Stretch With Hands Against Wall1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Stretching - Mobility/Calf Stretch With Hands Against Wall.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
ac555ce9-0895-4280-8b17-fbc8645a6c46	Chest dip	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	353a86d0-9f31-40d3-bfba-969ae615da15	1. Begin by grasping the parallel bars with your palms facing inward and your arms fully extended.\r\n2. Lift your body off the floor and lean slightly forward, crossing your ankles behind you.\r\n3. Lower your body by bending your elbows until your upper arms are parallel to the floor, keeping your chest leaning forward to engage your chest muscles.\r\n4. Push through your palms to extend your elbows and lift your body back to the starting position. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Focus on leaning forward slightly to emphasize the chest muscles rather than the triceps.\r\n2. Avoid locking your elbows at the top of the movement to keep tension on your muscles.\r\n3. Ensure your shoulders remain down and away from your ears to avoid unnecessary strain.	{"video_url": "videos/Chest/chest dip.mp4"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
91925a50-6abc-43cb-ac3c-9f19d95fcfe7	Calf stretch with rope	Resistance	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	de08e8c8-a4ec-465b-ae07-cc976f64cd81	1. Lie on the floor with your legs extended straight on the floor. Pass a rope with handles under your right forefoot, holding the handles with both hands.\r\n2. Keep your back flat against the floor and gently pull the rope towards you, flexing your foot and bringing your toes towards your shin.\r\n3. Straighten your leg fully to deepen the stretch in your calf muscle.\r\n4. Hold the stretch for 20-30 seconds, then release the rope and switch to the other foot, repeating the stretch.	1. Breathe deeply and steadily throughout the stretch to help relax your muscles.\r\n2. Use a moderate amount of tension on the rope to ensure a good stretch without causing discomfort or pain.\r\n3. Focus on feeling the stretch in your calf muscle, not your lower back or hamstrings.	{"video_url": "videos/Stretching - Mobility/Calf Stretch with Rope.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Stretching - Mobility/Calf Stretch with Rope1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Stretching - Mobility/Calf Stretch with Rope.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
