80cd554a-69a6-4b42-a0cc-df23df521627	Chest tap push up	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Begin in a plank position with your hands placed slightly wider than shoulder-width apart and your body forming a straight line from head to heels.\r\n2. Lower your body by bending your elbows until your chest is just above the floor, keeping your elbows at a 45-degree angle to your body.\r\n3. Explosively push through your palms to lift your body back up, lifting both hands off the floor at the top of the movement.\r\n4. While in the air, tap your chest with both hands, then quickly place your hands back on the floor and repeat the movement for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Perform the movement with control, especially when lowering your body, to prevent injury.\r\n2. Keep your feet slightly wider apart to enhance stability during the explosive push-up and chest tap.\r\n3. Focus on a strong, explosive push to lift your body and hands off the floor for the chest tap.	{"video_url": "videos/Chest/Chest Tap Push up.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Chest/Chest Tap Push up1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Chest/Chest Tap Push up.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
d8b14dbe-1c58-4146-b71c-b01ccac98464	Child pose	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Begin by kneeling on the floor with your knees together or slightly apart, and your big toes touching.\r\n2. Sit back on your heels, extending your arms forward on the floor, lowering your torso down between your thighs.\r\n3. Rest your forehead on the floor, keeping your arms extended out in front of you with palms facing down.\r\n4. Hold this position for the desired duration, breathing deeply and allowing your body to relax into the stretch.	1. Focus on breathing deeply and steadily, inhaling through your nose and exhaling through your mouth.\r\n2. Allow your hips to sink back towards your heels to deepen the stretch in your lower back and hips.\r\n3. If needed, you can place a cushion or folded blanket between your thighs and calves for added comfort.\r\n4. Keep your forehead resting on the floor or on a cushion to maintain a relaxed neck position.\r\n5. Use this pose as a gentle way to release tension and stretch the muscles in your back, hips, and shoulders.	{"video_url": "videos/Yoga/Child pose.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Yoga/Child pose1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Yoga/Child pose.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
939e5e1e-28dd-4e32-a1c6-4fe28b0bef02	Child pose up	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Begin on all fours with your hands directly under your shoulders and your knees under your hips. Keep your elbows bent close to your body with chest close to the floor.\r\n2. Push through your hands to lift your upper body slightly while simultaneously pushing your hips backwards towards your heels. Straighten your arms as you move your hips back.\r\n3. Continue to push your hips back until they are close to your heels, extending your arms fully in front of you on the floor.\r\n4. Hold this position for the desired duration, breathing deeply and allowing your body to relax into the stretch.	1. Focus on pushing your hips back towards your heels to deepen the stretch in your lower back and shoulders.\r\n2. Perform the movement slowly and with control to maximize the effectiveness of the stretch.\r\n3. Breathe deeply and steadily, inhaling as you lift your upper body and exhaling as you push your hips back.\r\n4. Use this pose to gently stretch and open up the muscles in your back, shoulders, and hips.	{"video_url": "videos/Yoga/child pose up.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Yoga/child pose up1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Yoga/child pose up.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
6129d7aa-6b58-4369-bbca-b134ad1546bb	Chin up	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	54938b47-43e8-47cd-9efc-18b4424e71e1	1. Begin by grasping a pull-up bar with an underhand grip (palms facing you) and your hands shoulder-width apart. Hang with your arms fully extended and your legs slightly bent or crossed behind you.\r\n2. Engage your core and pull your shoulder blades down and back to start the movement.\r\n3. Pull your body upward by bending your elbows and contracting your biceps, continuing until your chin is above the bar.\r\n4. Lower yourself back to the starting position with a controlled movement, fully extending your arms. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Focus on using your biceps and back muscles to lift your body, avoiding excessive momentum.\r\n2. Perform the movement slowly and with control, especially during the lowering phase, to maximize muscle activation and prevent injury.\r\n3. Ensure your shoulders remain down and away from your ears to avoid unnecessary strain.\r\n4. Breathe steadily throughout the exercise, exhaling as you pull up and inhaling as you lower yourself.\r\n5. Use a full range of motion by fully extending your arms at the bottom and bringing your chin above the bar at the top.	{"video_url": "videos/Back/chin up.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Back/chin up1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Back/chin up.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
