7c4ce7fe-dff7-4454-8686-4f7a362c25fc	Cobra side Ab stretch	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	de08e8c8-a4ec-465b-ae07-cc976f64cd81	1. Begin by lying face down on the floor with your legs extended straight behind you and your hands placed at shoulder level, palms flat on the floor.\r\n2. Press through your palms to lift your chest off the floor, straightening your arms to come into the cobra position, keeping your hips on the floor.\r\n3. From the cobra position, slowly rotate your torso to the right, looking over your right shoulder, and hold the stretch for a moment, feeling the stretch along the left side of your abdomen. Return to the center cobra position.\r\n4. Slowly rotate your torso to the left, looking over your left shoulder, and hold the stretch, feeling the stretch along the right side of your abdomen. Return to the center cobra position. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Focus on using your chest, shoulders, and triceps to push your body up while keeping your elbows close to your sides.\r\n2. Perform the movement with control to maximize muscle activation and prevent injury.\r\n3. Ensure your shoulders remain down and away from your ears to avoid unnecessary strain.\r\n4. Breathe steadily throughout the exercise, exhaling as you push up and lift your chest, and inhaling as you lower yourself and rotate.\r\n5. Keep your hips on the floor during the cobra and side stretches to maintain proper form and maximize the stretch in your lower back and sides.	{"video_url": "videos/Yoga/Cobra Side Ab Stretch.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Yoga/Cobra Side Ab Stretch1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Yoga/Cobra Side Ab Stretch.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
6ef5d953-d8ff-470a-be07-0cd16ece439b	Cobra yoga pose hold	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Begin by lying face down on the floor with your legs extended straight behind you and your hands placed at shoulder level, palms flat on the floor.\r\n2. Engage your core and press through your palms to lift your chest off the floor, straightening your arms to come into the cobra position, keeping your hips on the floor.\r\n3. Hold the cobra position, keeping your arms straight and your chest lifted, while breathing steadily.	1. Perform the movement with control, ensuring a smooth and steady rise into the cobra position.\r\n2. Ensure your shoulders remain down and away from your ears to avoid unnecessary strain.\r\n3. Breathe deeply and steadily throughout the exercise, inhaling as you lift your chest and exhaling as you hold the position.\r\n4. Keep your hips on the floor during the cobra hold to maintain proper form and maximize the stretch in your lower back and abdomen.	{"video_url": "videos/Yoga/cobra yoga pose hold.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Yoga/cobra yoga pose hold1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Yoga/cobra yoga pose hold.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
3ed0c446-69c8-48cf-a924-a5d76dc467e7	Cocoons	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Begin by lying flat on your back with your legs extended straight and your arms extended overhead on the floor.\r\n2. Engage your core and simultaneously lift your legs off the floor while bringing your arms forward to meet your knees, curling your body into a "cocoon" position.\r\n3. Hold the cocoon position for a moment, squeezing your core muscles.\r\n4. Slowly lower your legs and arms back to the starting position, maintaining control. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Focus on using your abdominal muscles to lift your legs and upper body, avoiding momentum.\r\n2. Use a mat or soft surface to support your back and prevent discomfort during the exercise.\r\n3. Ensure your lower back remains in contact with the floor as you lift and lower your legs to avoid unnecessary strain.\r\n4. Breathe steadily throughout the exercise, exhaling as you curl into the cocoon position and inhaling as you return to the starting position.\r\n	{"video_url": "videos/Stretching - Mobility/cocoons.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Stretching - Mobility/cocoons1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Stretching - Mobility/cocoons.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
c3049204-8c25-4ce9-aa26-7b82de183fbf	Commando pull-up	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	54938b47-43e8-47cd-9efc-18b4424e71e1	1. Begin by grasping a pull-up bar with both hands placed close together, palms facing each other in a neutral grip.\r\n2. Hang with your arms fully extended and your body straight. \r\n3. Engage your back and pull your body up towards the bar, leaning your head to one side of the bar as you lift.\r\n4. Lower yourself back to the starting position with a controlled movement. Repeat the pull-up, alternating the side of your head relative to the bar for each repetition.	1. Use a full range of motion by fully extending your arms at the bottom and bringing your head above the bar at the top.\r\n2. Perform the movement slowly and with control, especially during the lowering phase, to maximize muscle activation and prevent injury.\r\n3. Ensure your shoulders remain down and away from your ears to avoid unnecessary strain.\r\n4. Breathe steadily throughout the exercise, exhaling as you pull up and inhaling as you lower yourself.\r\n	{"video_url": "videos/Back/Commando Pull-up.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Back/Commando Pull-up1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Back/Commando Pull-up.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
