37feae22-79b3-4c79-82bf-22c1984efd0e	Control balance	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Lie down on your back, raise your legs towards the head, and hold your feet by extending your arms overhead.\r\n2. Release your right leg and take it upward until it becomes vertical to the floor.\r\n3. Place your free hand on your left calf and maintain balance.\r\n4. Hold for a while, return to the starting position, and repeat.	1. Perform the movement with control, especially when lifting and lowering your legs, to maximize muscle activation and prevent injury.\r\n2. Ensure your shoulders remain on the floor and avoid straining your neck.\r\n3. Breathe steadily throughout the exercise, exhaling as you lift your leg and inhaling as you lower it.\r\n4. Use a mat or soft surface to support your back and prevent discomfort during the exercise.	{"video_url": "videos/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Control Balance.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Control Balance1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Control Balance.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
