bee268a2-90e1-42bf-824d-8018b58a192c	Diagonal chop left	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Start standing with your feet shoulder-width apart, clasping your hands together and holding them extended opposite your chest.\r\n2. Rotate your torso and simultaneously bring your hands diagonally across your body towards your left hip, bending your knees slightly as you turn.\r\n3. Keep your arms extended and pivot your right foot as you rotate to protect your knee from strain.\r\n4. Return to the starting position in a controlled manner, bringing your hands back opposite your chest.	1. Engage your core throughout the movement to stabilize your spine and enhance power.\r\n2. Pivot on your feet during the rotation to ensure a full range of motion and to reduce stress on your knees.\r\n3. Focus on exhaling as you chop down and inhaling as you return to the starting position.\r\n4. Maintain a slight bend in your knees throughout the exercise to aid in balance and prevent strain on your joints.	{"video_url": "videos/Abdominals/diagonal chop left .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Abdominals/diagonal chop left.jpeg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
35c2def7-1c95-4b12-b720-f16981355cbf	Diagonal chop right	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Start standing with your feet shoulder-width apart, clasping your hands together and holding them extended oposite your chest.\r\n2. Rotate your torso and simultaneously bring your hands diagonally across your body towards your right hip, bending your knees slightly as you turn.\r\n3. Keep your arms extended and pivot your right foot as you rotate to protect your knee from strain.\r\n4. Return to the starting position in a controlled manner, bringing your hands back opposite your chest.	1. Engage your core throughout the movement to stabilize your spine and enhance power.\r\n2. Pivot on your feet during the rotation to ensure a full range of motion and to reduce stress on your knees.\r\n3. Focus on exhaling as you chop down and inhaling as you return to the starting position.\r\n4. Maintain a slight bend in your knees throughout the exercise to aid in balance and prevent strain on your joints.	{"video_url": "videos/Abdominals/diagonal chop right .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Abdominals/diagonal chop right.jpeg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
3b1b2da3-2dbc-411a-af1e-550fe75012c3	Diagonal lunge	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Stand with your feet together, arms extended outwards at shoulder level.\r\n2. Step diagonally forward with your right foot, planting it at a 45-degree angle. As you lower into a lunge, rotate your torso to the right and lean down to touch your right foot with your left hand, keeping your left leg straight.\r\n3. Press through your right heel and rotate back to center as you return to the starting position.\r\n4. Repeat the movement with your left leg, stepping diagonally forward, rotating left, and touching your left foot with your right hand.\r\n	1. Maintain your arms extended at shoulder level throughout the exercise to help with balance and increase the workout intensity.\r\n2. Rotate your torso smoothly and keep your movements controlled to avoid any jerky motions that might cause injury.\r\n3. Ensure that your lunging knee does not extend past your toes to protect your knee joint.	{"video_url": "videos/Legs/Diagonal Lunge.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Legs/Diagonal Lunge1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Legs/Diagonal Lunge.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
df0a3184-507b-44fa-be33-c9728fea2fb0	Diagonal opens	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart, arms bent at the elbows, elbows facing outwards, and hands close to your chest.\r\n2. Slide your right hand over your left forearm, both arms in an opposite diagonal direction while keeping the elbows bent.\r\n3. Return your hands to the starting position and repeat the movement by sliding your left hand over your right forearm, extending in the opposite diagonal direction.	1. Ensure your movements are smooth and controlled to maintain tension and focus on muscle engagement.\r\n2. Focus on maintaining a rhythmic breathing pattern, inhaling as you extend and exhaling as you return to the start position.\r\n3. Maintain a slight tension in your core throughout the exercise to help stabilize your upper body.\r\n	{"video_url": "videos/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Diagonal Opens.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Diagonal Opens1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Diagonal Opens.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
b15aa597-dbfa-4771-b162-49e7b73a7ba8	Diagonal punch	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart, knees slightly bent, and hands in a guard position near your face.\r\n2. Rotate your torso to the right, and extend your right arm in a diagonal punch across your body.\r\n3. Return your right hand to the starting position as you rotate your torso back to center.\r\n4. Repeat the motion with your left arm, rotating your torso to the left to execute a diagonal punch across your body.	1. Keep your hands up and elbows slightly bent when not punching to protect your face and maintain balance.\r\n2. Rotate your hips and shoulders fully with each punch to maximize power and engage your core muscles.\r\n3. Practice the punches slowly at first to ensure proper technique before increasing speed and power.\r\n4. Exhale sharply with each punch to increase force and stabilize your core.	{"video_url": "videos/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Diagonal Punch.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Diagonal Punch1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Diagonal Punch.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
e7fba936-f1f3-4c46-bb67-f33b06a04c75	Diamond push up	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Begin in a plank position with your hands close together under your chest, fingers forming a diamond shape (thumbs and index fingers touching).\r\n2. Lower your body towards the floor, keeping your elbows close to your body and your back straight.\r\n3. Pause briefly as your chest nearly touches your hands.\r\n4. Push back up to the starting plank position, maintaining a straight line from your head to your heels throughout the movement.	1. Ensure your elbows do not flare out; they should stay close to your body to maximize triceps engagement.\r\n2. Control your descent and ascent to increase muscle tension and enhance strength gains.\r\n3. Breathe in as you lower down and exhale forcefully as you push back up to help power the movement.\r\n4. Keep your head in a neutral position, aligned with your spine, to avoid neck strain.\r\n5. Perform the push-up at a slow to moderate pace to focus on form and muscle engagement without rushing.	{"video_url": "videos/Triceps/diamond push up  .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Triceps/diamond push up.jpeg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
b942d25d-1f00-49c1-a5aa-8111fd3af7dc	Diamond push-up (on knees)	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Begin by kneeling on a mat with your hands close together under your chest on the floor, fingers forming a diamond shape (thumbs and index fingers touching).\r\n2. Lean forward to shift your weight onto your hands while keeping your back straight and your core engaged.\r\n3. Lower your chest towards the floor by bending your elbows, keeping them close to your body.\r\n4. Press through your hands to lift your body back up to the starting position, maintaining the alignment of your spine throughout the movement.	1. Ensure your elbows point back rather than flaring out to the sides to maximize triceps activation and minimize shoulder strain.\r\n2. Keep your head and neck in a neutral position, aligned with your spine, to avoid any unnecessary strain.\r\n3. Breathe in as you lower yourself and exhale as you push back up, using your breath to help power the movement.	{"video_url": "videos/Triceps/Diamond Push-up (on knees).mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Triceps/Diamond Push-up (on knees).jpeg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
ecc894d0-f2ab-40bd-920e-516ed07d7d60	Dip leg raise on couch	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	0bcb2d29-e147-4deb-9a19-924da5ff89b3	1. Sit on the edge of a couch with your hands placed next to your hips, gripping the edge for support.\r\n2. Lift your hips off the couch by pressing down into your hands and straightening your arms, while keeping your feet flat on the floor and both knees bent.\r\n3. As you bend your elbows to lower your body into a dip, simultaneously lift one leg, bent at the knee, towards your chest.\r\n4. Push through your hands to raise your body back up, straightening your arms and simultaneously lowering your lifted leg back to the starting position.	1. Ensure your grip on the couch is secure to maintain balance and control throughout the exercise.\r\n2. Focus on a controlled, smooth motion both when lowering into the dip and lifting your body up to maximize muscle engagement.\r\n3. Keep the movement of your arms and legs coordinated; as you push up, lower the leg, and vice versa. 	{"video_url": "videos/Triceps/Dip Leg Raise on couch.mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Triceps/Dip Leg Raise on couch.jpeg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
9f5fea72-7ce8-413d-b1bb-91c0a267ef9f	Dip on floor with chair	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	353a86d0-9f31-40d3-bfba-969ae615da15	1. Sit on the floor with your back facing a chair and place your hands on the edge of the chair seat, fingers pointing towards your body.\r\n2. Bend your knees in front of you with your heels resting on the floor.\r\n3. Press down into the chair with your hands to lift your hips off the floor, straightening your arms.\r\n4. Bend your elbows to lower your body towards the floor until your elbows form about a 90-degree angle and push through your hands to lift your body back up to the starting position.	1. Ensure your hands are firmly placed on the chair and your fingers are well-aligned for a strong grip.\r\n2. Keep your movements controlled and steady to engage the triceps effectively and avoid any jerky movements.\r\n3. Avoid dipping too low to prevent shoulder strain; stopping at a 90-degree elbow angle is generally safe and effective.\r\n	{"video_url": "videos/Triceps/Dip on Floor with Chair.mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Triceps/Dip on Floor with Chair.jpeg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
ddbb4dd0-45ce-416d-8307-c8592a654e25	Dips between chairs	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	353a86d0-9f31-40d3-bfba-969ae615da15	1. Position two chairs parallel to each other, slightly wider than shoulder-width apart, with the seats facing away from you.\r\n2. Stand between the chairs and grasp the top of each chair back with your hands.\r\n3. Lift your body off the floor by straightening your arms, supporting your weight through your hands.\r\n4. Slowly lower your body by bending your elbows until they form about a 90-degree angle, keeping your body upright and close to the chair backs. Press through your hands to raise your body back to the starting position, extending your arms fully.	1. Check that the chairs are stable and strong enough to support your weight without tipping or moving.\r\n2. Keep your movements controlled and steady, focusing on using your triceps to lift and lower your body.\r\n3. Avoid locking your elbows at the top of the movement to keep tension on the muscles and protect your joints.	{"video_url": "videos/Triceps/Dips between Chairs.mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Triceps/Dips between Chairs.jpeg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
108869b9-720f-4b2a-b27b-c7a91ed0ff16	Donkey calf raise	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Stand on the edge of a step with your heels hanging off, placing your forefeet securely on the step.\r\n2. Lean forward and reach down to hold onto a bench in front of you for stability, keeping your back straight and hips aligned with your feet.\r\n3. Press down through your forefeet to elevate your heels as high as possible, fully contracting your calf muscles.\r\n4. Slowly lower your heels below the level of the step to maximize the stretch in your calves before the next lift.	1. Ensure your grip on the bench is secure to maintain balance and focus the effort on your calves.\r\n2. Keep your back flat and avoid rounding your shoulders to prevent unnecessary strain on your back.\r\n3. Emphasize the upward and downward movements equally to enhance muscle growth and strength in your calves.\r\n4. Maintain a slow, controlled pace to increase the intensity of the muscle contraction and effectiveness of the exercise.	{"video_url": "videos/Legs/Donkey Calf Raise.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Legs/Donkey Calf Raise1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Legs/Donkey Calf Raise.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
6a5479e1-418b-4338-b54e-14f20eddde4c	Donkey kicks bodyweight	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Begin on all fours in a tabletop position with your knees hip-width apart on the floor, hands under your shoulders, and your back flat.\r\n2. Keeping your knee bent at a 90-degree angle, lift your right leg up towards the ceiling, driving your heel upward as if pushing against the sky.\r\n3. Push your leg up until your thigh is in line with your body and your foot is above your knee.\r\n4. Lower your leg slowly back to the starting position without letting your knee touch the floor. Repeat the movement for the desired number of repetitions before switching to the left leg.	1. Ensure your movements are controlled and deliberate to maximize glute activation and minimize momentum.\r\n2. Keep your neck and spine in a neutral position by gazing down at the floor.\r\n3. Avoid swinging your leg or using jerky movements; the power should come from your glutes and not from momentum.\r\n	{"video_url": "videos/Legs/Donkey kicks bodyweight.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Legs/Donkey kicks bodyweight1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Legs/Donkey kicks bodyweight.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
19593860-6430-441c-aa24-daa46124608b	Doorway biceps curl	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Stand in a doorway and grip the sides of the door frame at about hip height, palms facing forward or slightly inward depending on comfort and doorway design.\r\n2. Step forward with one foot to create tension in your arms and lean slightly back, so your body weight helps create resistance.\r\n3. Curl your elbows to raise your body slowly towards the door frame, keeping your elbows pinned at your sides.\r\n4. Slowly extend your arms back to the starting position, repeat the movement.	1. Ensure your grip is firm and your hands are positioned comfortably to avoid strain on your wrists.\r\n2. Keep your body straight and avoid swinging; the motion should come solely from your biceps.\r\n3. Adjust the position of your feet to increase or decrease resistance—the further you step and lean back, the harder the curl.	{"video_url": "videos/Biceps/Doorway Biceps Curl.mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Biceps/Doorway Biceps Curl.jpeg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
41db104c-0070-45b7-8763-d373a11df60b	Double jump squat	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart and your hands close together in front of your torso. Lower into a squat position by bending your knees and hips, keeping your chest up and your weight in your heels. Stand back up to the starting position.\r\n2. Immediately lower into a squat again and then explosively jump up from the squat.\r\n3. Land softly on your feet after the jump, repeat the sequence.	1. Keep your chest up and back straight throughout the movement to maintain proper form and avoid injury.\r\n2. Perform the jumps in a fluid motion, transitioning smoothly between the squats and jumps.\r\n3. Focus on landing softly to reduce impact on your joints.	{"video_url": "videos/Legs/Double Jump Squat.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Legs/Double Jump Squat1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Legs/Double Jump Squat.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
5515d4a7-2442-4c1a-ba57-b8bf2dd68c86	Double knee drive	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart, both arms bent and raised by your sides.\r\n2. Lift your right knee towards your chest while rotating your torso to the right, bringing your left elbow to touch your right knee twice.\r\n3. Lower your right leg back to the starting position and return your torso to face forward.\r\n4. Repeat the movement on the opposite side by lifting your left knee towards your chest, rotating your torso to the left, and bringing your right elbow to touch your left knee twice. Continue alternating sides.	1. Keep your upper body upright and avoid leaning too far forward or backward to maintain balance and proper form.\r\n2. Engage your core muscles to stabilize your body and enhance the rotational movement.\r\n3. Focus on a steady, rhythmic breathing pattern, exhaling as you bring your knee and elbow together. 	{"video_url": "videos/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Double Knee Drive.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Double Knee Drive1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Double Knee Drive.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
