7f913faf-e027-4b4e-bde1-eba3366f60e0	Drag curl dumbbell	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	bfdb4696-9395-413b-bf0f-675c7a90d3be	1. Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart, holding a dumbbell in each hand with an underhand grip (palms facing up). Let your arms hang straight down by your sides.\r\n2. Begin by dragging the dumbbells upward along your torso by bending your elbows and pulling them back, as if you are zipping up your jacket.\r\n3. Continue lifting the dumbbells until they reach chest height, focusing on squeezing your biceps at the top of the movement.\r\n4. Slowly lower the dumbbells back to the starting position, maintaining control throughout the descent. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Focus on the mind-muscle connection, feeling the contraction in your biceps throughout the movement.\r\n2. Use a weight that allows you to perform the exercise with proper form without straining.\r\n3. Avoid using momentum; perform the exercise in a slow and controlled manner.	{"video_url": "videos/Biceps/drag curl dumbbell.mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Biceps/drag curl dumbbell.jpeg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
0c6a1570-3e53-4370-a833-34123236b3bd	Drag curl Resistance band	Resistance	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	0496ab82-eab1-4362-8dca-c3f5cd24f67f	1. Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart and place a resistance band under your feet. Hold the handles of the band with both hands, palms facing forward.\r\n2. Keep your elbows close to your body and your back straight. Start with your arms fully extended down at your sides.\r\n3. Curl the handles up by dragging your elbows along your torso, keeping them close to your torso, until your hands reach chest level.\r\n4. Slowly lower the handles back to the starting position with control. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Exhale as you curl the handles up and inhale as you lower them back down.\r\n2. Use a lighter resistance band if needed to ensure proper form and gradually increase the resistance as you get stronger.\r\n3. Focus on engaging your biceps throughout the movement.	{"video_url": "videos/Biceps/drag curl resistance band .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Biceps/drag curl resistance band.jpeg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
