0119e519-5878-470a-9ce7-81f5e9a65cdc	Dumbbell chest press decline	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	bfdb4696-9395-413b-bf0f-675c7a90d3be	1. Lie on a decline bench with your feet securely placed under the footpads. Hold a dumbbell in each hand with your arms fully extended above your chest, palms facing forward.\r\n2. Lower the dumbbells slowly towards your chest by bending your elbows, keeping your upper arms at a 45-degree angle to your body.\r\n3. Push the dumbbells back to the starting position by straightening your arms, squeezing your chest at the top of the movement.\r\n4. Repeat the movement for the desired number of repetitions, maintaining control throughout the exercise.	1. Ensure your feet are securely positioned under the footpads to prevent slipping during the movement.\r\n2. Maintain a steady and controlled motion, avoiding any jerking or sudden movements.\r\n3. Breathe in as you lower the dumbbells and exhale as you press them back up.	{"video_url": "videos/Chest/dumbbell chest press decline.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Chest/dumbbell chest press decline1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Chest/dumbbell chest press decline.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
d3f954c7-4201-4415-8763-4d9a846a1e67	Dumbbell chest press flat	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	bfdb4696-9395-413b-bf0f-675c7a90d3be	1. Lie flat on a bench with your feet firmly on the floor. Hold a dumbbell in each hand with your arms fully extended above your chest, palms facing forward.\r\n2. Lower the dumbbells slowly towards your chest by bending your elbows, keeping your upper arms at a 45-degree angle to your body.\r\n3. Push the dumbbells back to the starting position by straightening your arms, squeezing your chest at the top of the movement.\r\n4. Repeat the movement for the desired number of repetitions, maintaining control throughout the exercise.	1. Ensure your feet are flat on the floor to provide a solid base of support.\r\n2. Maintain a steady and controlled motion, avoiding any jerking or sudden movements.\r\n3. Breathe in as you lower the dumbbells and exhale as you press them back up.	{"image_male_end": "images/Chest/dumbbell chest press flat1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Chest/dumbbell chest press flat.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
