70e5da2f-5344-46f2-b671-2d95d5de8df3	Dumbbell squats to shoulder press	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	bfdb4696-9395-413b-bf0f-675c7a90d3be	1. Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart, holding a dumbbell in each hand at shoulder height just in front of your shoulders, palms facing each other.\r\n2. Lower into a squat by bending your knees and hips, keeping your back straight and chest up until your thighs are parallel to the floor.\r\n3. Push through your heels to stand up while simultaneously pressing the dumbbells overhead until your arms are fully extended.\r\n4. Lower the dumbbells back to shoulder height as you prepare for the next squat. Repeat the movement for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Ensure your knees do not extend past your toes during the squat to avoid unnecessary strain.\r\n2. Exhale as you press the dumbbells overhead and inhale as you lower into the squat.\r\n3. Keep your back straight and avoid leaning forward during the squat.	{"video_url": "videos/Legs/Dumbbell Squats to Shoulder Press  .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Legs/Dumbbell Squats to Shoulder Press  .jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
