b7044175-1cd5-449f-a0ee-55f1e1e06518	Exercise Ball Wall Squat	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart and place an exercise ball between your lower back and a wall. Lean slightly into the ball for support.\r\n2. Slowly lower your body into a squat position by bending your knees and hips, keeping your back straight and allowing the ball to roll along your back.\r\n3. Lower yourself until your thighs are parallel to the floor, ensuring your knees do not extend past your toes.\r\n4. Push through your heels to return to the starting position, straightening your legs. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Ensure your feet are positioned far enough in front of you so that your knees do not extend past your toes when squatting.\r\n2. Move slowly and with control to maximize muscle engagement and prevent injury.\r\n3. Focus on steady breathing, inhaling as you lower into the squat and exhaling as you push back up.\r\n4. Maintain an upright posture with your back against the ball to avoid leaning forward.	{"video_url": "videos/Legs/Exercise Ball Wall Squat.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Legs/Exercise Ball Wall Squat1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Legs/Exercise Ball Wall Squat.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
