6a1b0f97-f9bd-4365-8829-16afcbacfe2d	Extended Side Angle	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Stand with your feet wide apart, about 3-4 feet, with your right foot turned out 90 degrees and your left foot slightly turned in. Place your hands on your hips.\r\n2. Bend your right knee, ensuring it aligns over your right ankle, and lower your right thigh until it is parallel to the floor. Extend your left leg straight.\r\n3. Lean to your right side by bending your right knee further and place your right elbow on your right thigh. Raise your left arm overhead, creating a straight line from your left hand to your left foot.\r\n4. Hold the position for a moment, then return to the starting position with control. Repeat on the other side.	1. Ensure your bent knee is aligned with your ankle to avoid strain on the knee joint.\r\n2. Only stretch as far as is comfortable without causing pain or discomfort.\r\n3. Focus on deep, steady breathing, inhaling as you extend into the stretch and exhaling as you hold the stretch.\r\n4. Use a yoga block or modify the hand placement if needed for additional support.	{"video_url": "videos/Yoga/Extended Side Angle.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Yoga/Extended Side Angle1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Yoga/Extended Side Angle.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
296083cb-89cc-4980-8181-221ac5091e32	Extension And Inclination Neck Stretch	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Stand with your back straight and shoulders relaxed.\r\n2. Slowly rotate your head to the left side while diagonally lowering your head, bringing your chin towards your left shoulder to feel a stretch in your neck.\r\n3. Hold the stretch for a few seconds, breathing deeply and steadily.\r\n4. Return to the neutral position and repeat on the other side by rotating your head to the right and diagonally lowering your head towards your right shoulder. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Maintain good posture with your back straight and shoulders relaxed throughout the exercise.\r\n2. Perform the stretches in a smooth, fluid motion to enhance flexibility and reduce muscle tension.\r\n3. Avoid overextending your neck; only stretch as far as is comfortable without causing pain or discomfort.\r\n	{"video_url": "videos/Stretching - Mobility/Extension And Inclination Neck Stretch.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Stretching - Mobility/Extension And Inclination Neck Stretch1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Stretching - Mobility/Extension And Inclination Neck Stretch.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
f3f8b864-5f36-4fd6-9f47-27fce9bc2e4b	Extension Of Arms In Vertical Stretch	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart, your back straight, and your core engaged.\r\n2. Raise your arms overhead, interlocking your fingers and turning your palms upward.\r\n3. Stretch upwards as much as possible, lengthening your spine and reaching towards the ceiling. Hold the position for 15-30 seconds.\r\n4. Slowly release the stretch and bring your arms back down to your sides. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Move slowly and with control to maximize the stretch and avoid any sudden movements.\r\n2. Focus on deep, steady breathing, inhaling as you reach upwards and exhaling as you hold the stretch.\r\n3. Avoid arching your back; instead, focus on lengthening your spine.	{"video_url": "videos/Stretching - Mobility/Extension Of Arms In Vertical Stretch.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Stretching - Mobility/Extension Of Arms In Vertical Stretch1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Stretching - Mobility/Extension Of Arms In Vertical Stretch.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
