9463c739-53ec-438e-aba0-ab12cd57431d	Fire hydrant bodyweight	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Begin on the floor in an all-fours position with your hands directly under your shoulders and your knees under your hips. Keep your back straight and your core engaged.\r\n2. Keeping your knee bent at a 90-degree angle, lift your right leg out to the side until your thigh is parallel to the floor. Keep your hips level and avoid rotating your torso.\r\n3. Hold the position for a moment, then lower your right leg back to the starting position with control.\r\n4. Repeat the movement for the desired number of repetitions, then switch to your left leg and repeat.	1. Avoid rotating your hips or torso; focus on isolating the movement in your hip.\r\n2. Perform the exercise on a stable, non-slip surface to prevent slipping or injury.\r\n3. Breathe steadily, exhaling as you lift your leg and inhaling as you lower it.\r\n4. Ensure your hands are positioned directly under your shoulders to maintain proper form and prevent strain.\r\n	{"video_url": "videos/Legs/fire hydrant bodyweight  .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Legs/fire hydrant bodyweight  .jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
1891dbfa-ea53-4431-b532-39f3d54098b4	Fire hydrant circle bodyweight	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Begin on the floor in an all-fours position with your hands directly under your shoulders and your knees under your hips. Keep your back straight and your core engaged.\r\n2. Keeping your knee bent at a 90-degree angle, lift your right leg out to the side until your thigh is parallel to the floor.\r\n3. Move your right leg in a circular motion, making small controlled circles with your knee while keeping your hips level and avoiding torso rotation.\r\n4. Complete the desired number of circles, then lower your right leg back to the starting position. Repeat on the left side.	1. Avoid rotating your hips or torso; focus on isolating the movement in your hip.\r\n2. Perform the exercise on a stable, non-slip surface to prevent slipping or injury.\r\n3. Breathe steadily, exhaling as you lift your leg and inhaling as you lower it.\r\n4. Ensure your hands are positioned directly under your shoulders to maintain proper form and prevent strain.\r\n	{"video_url": "videos/Legs/fire hydrant circle bodyweight.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Legs/fire hydrant circle bodyweight1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Legs/fire hydrant circle bodyweight.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
8c479052-82db-477f-868b-b19bed43e34d	Fixed bar stretch	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	35516b5e-1db4-4a4c-84d8-d7845b9c83f1	1. Stand facing a fixed vertical bar. Position your feet shoulder-width apart and grasp the bar with both hands, palms facing each other.\r\n2. Step back slightly and lean your hips backward, allowing your arms to extend fully and your upper body to lean forward. Keep your back straight and your knees bent.\r\n3. Lean backwards and down to the floor while pulling back with your hips to feel a deep stretch in your shoulders, upper back, and lats.\r\n4. Hold the stretch for 15-30 seconds, breathing deeply and steadily. Slowly return to the starting position by stepping forward and releasing the bar.	1. Move slowly and with control to maximize the stretch and avoid any sudden movements.\r\n2. Only stretch as far as is comfortable without causing pain or discomfort.\r\n3. Ensure the bar is securely fixed and can support your weight.	{"video_url": "videos/Stretching - Mobility/fixed bar stretch  .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Stretching - Mobility/fixed bar stretch  .jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
