7253459f-b6c1-45f1-b3e2-ff89c9ab819d	Hollow hold	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Lie on your back with your legs extended and your arms stretched overhead.\r\n2. Engage your core and lift your shoulders and legs off the floor, keeping your lower back pressed into the floor. Your body should form a slight curve with your arms and legs elevated.\r\n3. Hold this position, maintaining tension in your core and keeping your lower back flat against the floor.\r\n4. Continue to hold the position for the desired duration, then slowly lower your shoulders and legs back to the starting position.	1. Ensure your shoulders and legs are lifted at the same height to create a balanced position.\r\n2. Focus on steady breathing, inhaling through your nose and exhaling through your mouth to help maintain focus and endurance.\r\n3. If the full hollow hold is too challenging, you can modify the position by bending your knees or keeping your arms by your sides.\r\n4. Avoid straining your neck; keep it relaxed and in line with your spine.	{"video_url": "videos/Abdominals/hollow hold .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Abdominals/hollow hold.jpeg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
b4c3fac3-d840-44ed-8cc1-e36d708efafe	In and out squats jump bodyweight	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Stand tall with your back straight, feet shoulder-width apart, and clasp your hands in front of your chest.\r\n2. Lower your hips, jump up and land into a squat position with your knees bent, thighs parallel to the floor, and feet placed wider than your shoulder width.\r\n3. Then lower your hips again, jump up, and land into a squat position with your knees bent, thighs parallel to the floor, and feet placed hip-width apart this time.\r\n4. Repeat by jumping in and out alternately.	1. Land softly on your forefeet to reduce impact on your joints.\r\n2. Ensure your knees are aligned with your toes when you squat to avoid strain.\r\n3. Move quickly but with control to maximize the effectiveness of the exercise and prevent injury.	{"video_url": "videos/Legs/in and out squats jump bodyweight  .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Legs/in and out squats jump bodyweight  .jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
cfb922f9-bcea-45ad-8677-25ddd4dabcca	In and out squats jump bodyweight (2)	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Stand tall with your back straight, feet shoulder-width apart, and clasp your hands in front of your chest.\r\n2. Lower your hips, jump up and land into a squat position with your knees bent, thighs parallel to the floor, and feet placed wider than your shoulder width.\r\n3. Then lower your hips again, jump up, and land into a squat position with your knees bent, thighs parallel to the floor, and feet placed hip-width apart this time.\r\n4. Repeat by jumping in and out alternately.	1. Land softly on your forefeet to reduce impact on your joints.\r\n2. Ensure your knees are aligned with your toes when you squat to avoid strain.\r\n3. Move quickly but with control to maximize the effectiveness of the exercise and prevent injury.	{"video_url": "videos/Legs/in and out squats jump bodyweight (2).mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Legs/in and out squats jump bodyweight (2)1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Legs/in and out squats jump bodyweight (2).jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
6e207771-945a-4775-bed8-599566009fcb	Incline bench cable fly	Resistance	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	7c8ccea6-1ecd-4abd-a28f-2f05d0d539a5	1. Set an incline bench between two cable machines with the pulleys positioned at the middle setting. Lie back on the bench with your feet flat on the floor. Grasp a handle in each hand, with your palms facing up and your arms extended to your sides.\r\n2. Keep a slight bend in your elbows and your back pressed firmly against the bench.\r\n3. Raise the handles opposite your chest in a wide arc, until your arms are level with your chest, squeezing your chest muscles at the top of the movement.\r\n4. Lower the handles back the starting position in a controlled manner. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Keep a slight bend in your elbows throughout the exercise to avoid straining your joints.\r\n2. Keep your back and head pressed firmly against the bench.\r\n3. Exhale as you bring the handles up and inhale as you lower them down.	{"video_url": "videos/Chest/incline bench cable fly.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Chest/incline bench cable fly1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Chest/incline bench cable fly.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
66b66109-bb04-450c-b029-ebdca1feb7df	Incline diamond push up on bench	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Position yourself facing a bench. Place your hands on the edge of the bench close together so that your thumbs and index fingers form a diamond shape.\r\n2. Step your feet back to extend your legs fully, keeping your body in a straight line from head to heels. Engage your core to maintain stability.\r\n3. Lower your chest towards the bench by bending your elbows, keeping them close to your body.\r\n4. Push through your hands to extend your arms and return to the starting position. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Move slowly and with control to maximize muscle engagement and prevent injury.\r\n2. Focus on steady breathing, exhaling as you push up and inhaling as you lower down.\r\n3. Avoid flaring your elbows out to the sides; keep them close to your body to engage your triceps more effectively.\r\n4. Use a stable, non-slip bench to prevent any movement or slipping during the exercise.	{"video_url": "videos/Triceps/incline diamond push up On Bench.mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Triceps/incline diamond push up On Bench.jpeg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
49ef086a-633e-40b9-9c40-de2059e46756	Incline dumbbell curl	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	bfdb4696-9395-413b-bf0f-675c7a90d3be	1. Set an adjustable bench to a 45-degree incline and sit back against it with your feet flat on the floor. Hold a dumbbell in each hand with your arms fully extended down by your sides, palms facing forward (supinated grip).\r\n2. Engage your core and keep your elbows close to your torso. Slowly curl both dumbbells up towards your shoulders simultaneously, maintaining the supinated grip with your palms facing upward.\r\n3. Squeeze your biceps at the top of the movement, then slowly lower the dumbbells back to the starting position with control.\r\n4. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Focus on a full range of motion, ensuring you fully extend your arms at the bottom of each curl.\r\n2. Maintain a slight bend in your elbows at the start to avoid locking them out.\r\n3. Keep your upper arms stationary and close to your torso to isolate the biceps effectively.	{"video_url": "videos/Biceps/incline dumbbell curl.mp4"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
4a1c4480-2c9f-4e9e-9c3f-a83a4e8a9962	Incline lateral raises dumbbell	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	bfdb4696-9395-413b-bf0f-675c7a90d3be	1. Adjust an incline bench to a 45-degree angle and lie chest-first against it, with your feet firmly planted on the floor for stability.\r\n2. Hold a dumbbell in each hand with a neutral grip (palms facing each other), allowing the dumbbells to hang down towards the floor in line with your shoulders.\r\n3. Keeping your arms slightly bent at the elbows, raise the dumbbells up and out to the sides until they reach shoulder height.\r\n4. Lower the dumbbells back to the starting position with control. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Maintain a slight bend in your elbows throughout the movement to reduce joint strain.\r\n2. Keep your body stabilized against the bench to isolate your shoulder muscles.\r\n3. Use a slow and controlled motion to maximize muscle engagement.	{"video_url": "videos/Shoulders/incline lateral raises dumbbell.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Shoulders/incline lateral raises dumbbell1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Shoulders/incline lateral raises dumbbell.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
d794066a-f9dc-4d62-9a7a-1564c9b2d77b	Intermediate hip flexor and quad stretch	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	de08e8c8-a4ec-465b-ae07-cc976f64cd81	1. Lie on your stomach with your legs extended and your arms at your sides. Position an elastic cable around your right ankle.\r\n2. Bend your right knee to bring your foot towards your glutes, holding the elastic cable in your both hands.\r\n3. Gently pull on the cable to bring your foot closer to your glutes, feeling the stretch in your quadriceps. Hold this position for a moment.\r\n4. Extend your right leg lightly backwards, allowing the cable to provide resistance and deepen the stretch in your hip flexor and quadriceps. Repeat the movement for the desired number of repetitions, then switch to the left leg.	1. Focus on deep, steady breathing, inhaling as you extend your leg and exhaling as you pull your foot towards your glutes.\r\n2. If you find it difficult to reach the cable, use a longer strap or adjust the tension to ensure a comfortable stretch.\r\n3. Ensure your head and neck remain in a neutral position, looking down towards the floor to avoid strain.\r\n4. Perform the stretch on a comfortable surface, such as a yoga mat, to prevent discomfort or injury.	{"video_url": "videos/Stretching - Mobility/intermediate hip flexor and quad stretch.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Stretching - Mobility/intermediate hip flexor and quad stretch1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Stretching - Mobility/intermediate hip flexor and quad stretch.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
6b4388bf-6b84-4371-8f46-f171eb5e556c	Inverted rows on smith machine	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	132c52b1-6336-4426-a457-c35a314038f2	1. Position a bar on the smith machine at about waist height. Lie on your back underneath the bar with your legs extended and your heels on the floor.\r\n2. Grasp the bar with an overhand grip, hands slightly wider than shoulder-width apart.\r\n3. Engage your core and pull your chest towards the bar by bending your elbows, keeping your body in a straight line from head to heels.\r\n4. Lower yourself back to the starting position with control. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Focus on using your back muscles to pull yourself up, rather than your arms.\r\n2. Adjust the height of the bar or your foot position to make the exercise easier or harder as needed.\r\n3. Breathe steadily, exhaling as you pull up and inhaling as you lower yourself down.\r\n4. Ensure the bar is securely locked in place on the smith machine to prevent any movement.\r\n	{"video_url": "videos/Back/inverted rows on smith machine.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Back/inverted rows on smith machine1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Back/inverted rows on smith machine.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
a1554d53-5fec-4469-b5ce-9c62a255d1c6	Iron cross stretch	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Lie on your back with your arms extended out to your sides, forming a T-shape, and your legs extended straight.\r\n2. Lift your right leg towards the ceiling, keeping it straight, and then lower it across your body towards your left hand while keeping your shoulders flat on the floor.\r\n3. Allow your right leg to lower as far as comfortably possible, feeling a stretch in your lower back, glutes, and hamstrings.\r\n4. Hold the stretch for 15-30 seconds, then slowly return your right leg to the starting position. Repeat on the other side with your left leg.	1. Only stretch as far as is comfortable without causing pain or discomfort.\r\n2. Perform the stretch on a comfortable surface, such as a yoga mat, to prevent discomfort or injury.\r\n3. If you have limited flexibility, bend your knee slightly to reduce strain and gradually work towards straightening your leg.	{"video_url": "videos/Stretching - Mobility/iron cross stretch.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Stretching - Mobility/iron cross stretch1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Stretching - Mobility/iron cross stretch.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
3f1aaa4a-5d42-4fff-a2c8-598cf142474e	Iso Lateral Shoulder Press Alternate Arms	Resistance	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	1a636d29-2aec-4f45-914e-8fab15563d39	1. Sit on the Iso-Lateral Shoulder Press machine, back pressed against the backrest and feet flat on the floor. Grasp the handles with both hands, palms facing forward.\r\n2. Press one handle upward by extending your arm fully while keeping the other arm stationary.\r\n3. Squeeze your shoulder muscles at the top of the movement and slowly return the handle to the starting position with control.\r\n4. Repeat with the other arm, alternating arms for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Keep your back pressed against the backrest throughout the exercise.\r\n2. Focus on engaging your shoulder muscles throughout the movement.\r\n3. Exhale as you press the handle upward and inhale as you return it to the starting position.	{"video_url": "videos/Shoulders/Iso Lateral Shoulder Press Alternate Arms.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Shoulders/Iso Lateral Shoulder Press Alternate Arms1.jpg", "image_female_end": "images/Shoulders/Iso Lateral Shoulder Press Alternate Arms_Female1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Shoulders/Iso Lateral Shoulder Press Alternate Arms.jpg", "image_female_start": "images/Shoulders/Iso Lateral Shoulder Press Alternate Arms_Female.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
