6a889223-3c48-457c-a4be-f6f92943b509	Jack knives	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Lie flat on your back with your legs extended and your arms stretched on your sides.\r\n2. Simultaneously lift your upper body and legs towards each other, reaching your hands towards your feet. Engage your core to lift both your torso and legs.\r\n3. Try to touch your hands to your feet at the top of the movement, forming a "V" shape with your body.\r\n4. Slowly lower your upper body and legs back to the starting position with control. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. If the full movement is too challenging, modify by bending your knees slightly.\r\n2. Focus on steady breathing, exhaling as you lift your body and inhaling as you lower it.\r\n3. Ensure your lower back remains pressed into the floor during the movement to prevent strain.	{"video_url": "videos/Abdominals/jack knives .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Abdominals/jack knives.jpeg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
06c4346b-5ff9-43a7-97b9-e631941b47f9	Jump Rope alternating foot	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	ecbf4b6a-ecec-4ea8-a7d2-4e389d03d2e1	1. Stand with your feet together, holding a jump rope with the handles in each hand. Position the rope behind you, ready to swing it over your head.\r\n2. Swing the rope over your head and, as it passes under your feet, lift one foot off the floor, quickly followed by the other foot, allowing the rope to pass beneath both feet in succession.\r\n3. Continue to alternate feet with each jump, lifting one foot after the other, maintaining a steady rhythm and keeping your jumps low and controlled.\r\n4. Repeat the movement for the desired duration or number of repetitions, ensuring a smooth and continuous motion.	1. Focus on quick, controlled movements, keeping your jumps low to minimize impact on your joints.\r\n2. Use your wrists to swing the rope, rather than your arms, to maintain a smooth and efficient motion.\r\n3. Wear supportive footwear to protect your feet and ankles during the exercise.	{"video_url": "videos/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Jump Rope alternating foot.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Jump Rope alternating foot1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Jump Rope alternating foot.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
8967fa9f-b047-4c35-a8b5-f263c328c913	Jump Rope basic jump	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	ecbf4b6a-ecec-4ea8-a7d2-4e389d03d2e1	1. Stand with your feet together, holding a jump rope with the handles in each hand. Position the rope behind you, ready to swing it over your head.\r\n2. Swing the rope over your head and, as it passes under your feet, jump with both feet simultaneously, keeping your jumps low to the floor.\r\n3. Land softly on your forefeet and immediately swing the rope over your head again for the next jump.\r\n4. Continue jumping at a steady rhythm, maintaining a smooth and continuous motion for the desired duration or number of repetitions.	1. Focus on quick, controlled movements, keeping your jumps low to minimize impact on your joints.\r\n2. Use your wrists to swing the rope, rather than your arms, to maintain a smooth and efficient motion.\r\n3. Wear supportive footwear to protect your feet and ankles during the exercise.	{"video_url": "videos/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Jump Rope basic jump.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Jump Rope basic jump1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Jump Rope basic jump.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
fc13db5a-74d8-4d38-9879-db31d253c8f0	Jump Rope double bounce	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	ecbf4b6a-ecec-4ea8-a7d2-4e389d03d2e1	1. Stand with your feet together, holding a jump rope with the handles in each hand. Position the rope behind you, ready to swing it over your head.\r\n2. Swing the rope over your head and, as it passes under your feet, perform a small jump, landing on your forefeet.\r\n3. Immediately perform a second smaller bounce while keeping the rope in motion and preparing for the next swing.\r\n4. Continue with the double bounce rhythm, maintaining a smooth and controlled motion for the desired duration or number of repetitions.	1. Focus on quick, controlled movements, keeping your jumps low to minimize impact on your joints.\r\n2. Use your wrists to swing the rope, rather than your arms, to maintain a smooth and efficient motion.\r\n3. Wear supportive footwear to protect your feet and ankles during the exercise.	{"video_url": "videos/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Jump Rope double bounce.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Jump Rope double bounce1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Jump Rope double bounce.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
23e11c2d-1f30-41d3-af29-e8ad1d49193b	Jump Rope face pull	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	ecbf4b6a-ecec-4ea8-a7d2-4e389d03d2e1	1. Loop the jump rope over a vertical bar or similar stable structure, ensuring the rope is at about hip height. Stand facing the bar with your feet shoulder-width apart, holding the handles of the jump rope with both hands.\r\n2. Step back slightly to create tension in the rope, keeping your core engaged and your back straight.\r\n3. Pull the rope towards your face by bending your elbows and bringing your hands towards your ears, engaging your upper back and shoulder muscles.\r\n4. Extend your arms back out to the starting position with control. Repeat the movement for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Focus on squeezing your shoulder blades together as you pull the rope towards your face to maximize muscle engagement.\r\n2. Move slowly  with control and avoid using momentum to prevent injury.\r\n3. Breathe steadily, exhaling as you pull the rope towards your face and inhaling as you extend your arms back out.\r\n4. Ensure the vertical bar or structure is stable and can support the tension in the rope to prevent slipping or injury.	{"video_url": "videos/Shoulders/Jump Rope face pull.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Shoulders/Jump Rope face pull1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Shoulders/Jump Rope face pull.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
a07bb710-1f45-4778-90ae-8d896817e8ea	Jump Rope row	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	ecbf4b6a-ecec-4ea8-a7d2-4e389d03d2e1	1. Loop the jump rope over a vertical bar or similar stable structure, ensuring the rope is at about hip height. Stand facing the bar with your feet shoulder-width apart, holding the handles of the jump rope with both hands.\r\n2. Step back slightly to create tension in the rope, keeping your core engaged and your back straight.\r\n3. Pull the rope towards your torso by bending your elbows and bringing your hands towards your sides, engaging your upper back and shoulder muscles.\r\n4. Extend your arms back out to the starting position with control. Repeat the movement for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Focus on squeezing your shoulder blades together as you pull the rope towards your torso to maximize muscle engagement.\r\n2. Ensure the vertical bar or structure is stable and can support the tension in the rope to prevent slipping or injury.\r\n3. Breathe steadily, exhaling as you pull the rope towards your torso and inhaling as you extend your arms back out.	{"video_url": "videos/Back/Jump Rope row.mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Back/Jump Rope row female.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
bb0cd140-c7b7-40fe-a4b0-d84bb49221c0	Jump squats bodyweight	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart and your arms at your sides.\r\n2. Lower your body into a squat position by bending your knees and pushing your hips back, keeping your chest up and your core engaged.\r\n3. Explosively jump up, extending your legs fully and swinging your arms up for momentum.\r\n4. Land softly back into the squat position with your knees bent and your hips pushed back. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Land softly on your forefeet to reduce impact on your joints.\r\n2. Ensure your knees are aligned with your toes when you squat to avoid strain.\r\n3. Move quickly but with control to maximize the effectiveness of the exercise and prevent injury.	{"video_url": "videos/Legs/Jump Squats bodyweight  .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Legs/Jump Squats bodyweight  .jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
03417f59-7d79-4639-80d7-3cfee3fa6c9f	Jumping jack	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Stand with your feet together and your arms at your sides.\r\n2. Jump your feet out to the sides while simultaneously raising your arms overhead, forming an "X" shape with your body.\r\n3. Quickly jump back to the starting position with your feet together and your arms at your sides.\r\n4. Repeat the movement for the desired duration or number of repetitions, maintaining a steady rhythm.	1. Maintain a slight bend in your knees throughout the exercise to absorb impact and reduce strain on your joints.\r\n2. Keep your movements light and quick to enhance cardiovascular benefits.\r\n3. Engage your shoulders and back muscles when raising your arms to ensure full range of motion.\r\n4. Keep your gaze forward and your head in a neutral position to maintain alignment.	{"video_url": "videos/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/jumping jack  .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/jumping jack  .jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
7fd55b15-b714-41de-b803-9dab26446918	Kettlebell bulgarian split squat right side view	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	7352a8b5-30da-44d7-9cae-8a031f5d2aed	1. Stand facing away from a bench, holding a kettlebell in each hand with arms hanging by your sides. Place your left foot on the bench behind you.\r\n2. Keep your right foot firmly planted on the floor and lower your body by bending your right knee, descending until your right thigh is parallel to the floor.\r\n3. Press through your right heel to return to the starting position, straightening your leg.\r\n4. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Ensure your front knee does not extend past your toes during the descent.\r\n2. Focus on keeping your torso upright; avoid leaning forward excessively.\r\n3. Exhale as you push up to the starting position and inhale as you lower your body.	{"video_url": "videos/Legs/kettlebell bulgarian split squat right side view  .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Legs/kettlebell bulgarian split squat right side view  .jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
0b8001bc-6885-4533-a3b1-6528ad96d69b	Kettlebell half kneeling shoulder press	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	7352a8b5-30da-44d7-9cae-8a031f5d2aed	1. Begin in a half-kneeling position with your right knee on the floor and your left foot flat on the floor in front of you. Hold a kettlebell in your right hand, racked at shoulder height with your elbow bent, facing the floor, and close to your body.\r\n2. Press the kettlebell overhead by extending your right arm fully, keeping your wrist straight and in line with your shoulder.\r\n3. Lower the kettlebell back to the starting position with control.\r\n4. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Ensure your knee and hip are aligned, maintaining a 90-degree angle in both legs.\r\n2. Press the kettlebell straight up, avoiding any forward or backward motion.\r\n3. Exhale as you press the kettlebell overhead and inhale as you lower it back down.	{"video_url": "videos/Shoulders/kettlebell half kneeling shoulder press .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Shoulders/kettlebell half kneeling shoulder press .jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
b3b4305a-f5da-43f2-b86b-9ec58ad465bf	Kettlebell kneeling one arm shoulder press	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	7352a8b5-30da-44d7-9cae-8a031f5d2aed	1. Begin in a kneeling position on both knees with your torso upright. Hold a kettlebell in your right hand at shoulder height, with your elbow bent, facing the floor, and close to your body.\r\n2. Press the kettlebell overhead by extending your right arm fully, keeping your wrist straight and aligned with your shoulder.\r\n3. Lower the kettlebell back to the starting position.\r\n4. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Maintain a neutral spine throughout the movement.\r\n2. Press the kettlebell straight up, avoiding any forward or backward motion.\r\n3. Exhale as you press the kettlebell overhead and inhale as you lower it back down.	{"video_url": "videos/Shoulders/kettlebell kneeling one arm shoulder press .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Shoulders/kettlebell kneeling one arm shoulder press .jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
6852427f-215c-4ec2-bc5a-a48578ad5342	Kettlebell seesaw press	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	7352a8b5-30da-44d7-9cae-8a031f5d2aed	1. Begin in a standing position with your feet shoulder-width apart, holding a kettlebell in each hand at shoulder height. Your elbows should be bent, facing the floor and your palms facing inward.\r\n2. Press the kettlebell in your right hand overhead by extending your right arm fully while slightly leaning your torso to your left side.\r\n3. Lower the right kettlebell back to shoulder height and then press the kettlebell in your left hand overhead by extending your left arm fully and slightly leaning your torso to the right side.\r\n4. Continue alternating the presses for the desired number of repetitions.\r\n	1. Press each kettlebell straight up, avoiding any forward or backward motion.\r\n2. Exhale as you press each kettlebell overhead and inhale as you lower it back down.\r\n3. Ensure your wrists stay straight and aligned with your forearms to prevent strain.	{"video_url": "videos/Shoulders/Kettlebell Seesaw Press.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Shoulders/Kettlebell Seesaw Press1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Shoulders/Kettlebell Seesaw Press.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
b4a0e124-1b7a-4d28-8ba5-59a4d8369ee7	Kettlebell single arm clean and press	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	7352a8b5-30da-44d7-9cae-8a031f5d2aed	1. Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart and the kettlebell placed on the floor between your feet. Bend your knees and hinge at your hips to grab the kettlebell with your right hand.\r\n2. Explosively extend your hips and knees to lift the kettlebell off the floor and swing it up to shoulder height. As the kettlebell rises, rotate your wrist to catch it in a rack position with your elbow bent and close to your body.\r\n3. Press the kettlebell overhead by extending your right arm fully, keeping your wrist straight and aligned with your shoulder.\r\n4. Lower the kettlebell back to the rack position with control, then return it to the starting position on the floor. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions, then switch to the left hand.	1. Use your hips and legs to generate power for the clean.\r\n2. Use an appropriate weight to maintain proper form and control.\r\n3. Keep your wrist straight and aligned with your forearm during the press.	{"video_url": "videos/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Kettlebell Single Arm Clean and Press.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Kettlebell Single Arm Clean and Press1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Kettlebell Single Arm Clean and Press.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
eee05944-f391-4a3e-8e4d-2148e1f08d0a	Kettlebell single leg glute bridge pullover	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	7352a8b5-30da-44d7-9cae-8a031f5d2aed	1. Lie on your back with your knees bent and feet flat on the floor, holding a kettlebell with both hands extended straight on the floor. Extend your right leg upwards bent at 90 degrees.\r\n2. Press through your left heel to lift your hips off the floor, forming a straight line from your shoulders to your left knee. Simultaneously, extend the kettlebell overhead with both arms, keeping a slight bend in your elbows.\r\n3. Lower your hips back to the floor while bringing the kettlebell back to the starting position.\r\n4. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions, then switch to your left leg extended and perform the same motion.	1. Lower the kettlebell and your hips in a controlled manner to prevent any sudden movements or loss of balance.\r\n2. Focus on squeezing your glutes at the top of the bridge for maximum activation.\r\n3. Inhale as you lower your hips and the kettlebell, and exhale as you lift them.	{"video_url": "videos/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Kettlebell Single Leg Glute Bridge Pullover.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Kettlebell Single Leg Glute Bridge Pullover1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Kettlebell Single Leg Glute Bridge Pullover.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
a8451566-7c26-47e8-b4a1-2282ed3a914d	Kettlebell split squat	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	7352a8b5-30da-44d7-9cae-8a031f5d2aed	1. Stand with your feet hip-width apart, holding a kettlebell in each hand with your arms hanging by your sides. Take a step forward with your right foot and position your left foot back, standing on the ball of your left foot.\r\n2. Bend both knees to lower your body into a split squat. Your back knee should hover just above the floor, and your front thigh should be parallel to the floor.\r\n3. Push through your right heel to return to the starting position, fully extending both legs.\r\n4. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions, then switch legs and perform the same number of repetitions on the other side.	1. Keep your chest up and your back straight throughout the movement.\r\n2. Ensure your front knee stays aligned with your ankle, not extending past your toes.\r\n3. Keep your feet hip-width apart to maintain proper alignment and balance.	{"video_url": "videos/Legs/Kettlebell Split squat.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Legs/Kettlebell Split squat1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Legs/Kettlebell Split squat.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
13a61793-36f0-4d6b-8800-f4706331a8f2	Kettlebell squats	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	7352a8b5-30da-44d7-9cae-8a031f5d2aed	1. Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart, holding a kettlebell with each hand hanging by your sides.\r\n2. Lower your body into a squat by bending your knees and pushing your hips back as if sitting in a chair.\r\n3. Continue lowering yourself until your thighs are parallel to the floor, making sure your knees track over your toes.\r\n4. Push through your heels to stand back up to the starting position, fully extending your legs.	1. Ensure your knees stay in line with your toes to prevent any inward collapse.\r\n2. Inhale as you lower into the squat and exhale as you push back up to standing.\r\n3. Focus on pressing through your heels to activate your glutes and quadriceps.	{"video_url": "videos/Legs/kettlebell squats  .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Legs/kettlebell squats  .jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
883f6262-d733-4d2c-b53d-073269077888	Kettlebell Standing Bottoms-up One Arm Shoulder Press	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	7352a8b5-30da-44d7-9cae-8a031f5d2aed	1. Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart, holding a kettlebell in your right hand with the bell facing up (bottoms-up position). Place your  left hand on your hip.\r\n2. Press the kettlebell overhead by extending your elbow, keeping your wrist straight.\r\n3. Once your arm is fully extended overhead, pause for a second to fully activate the shoulder muscles.\r\n4. Slowly lower the kettlebell back to the starting position with control, keeping the bottoms-up orientation throughout the movement. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Maintain a strong grip on the kettlebell to keep it stable in the bottoms-up position.\r\n2. Start with a lighter weight to master the balance and control required for the bottoms-up position.\r\n3. Avoid locking your elbow completely at the top of the press to protect your joint.	{"video_url": "videos/Shoulders/Kettlebell Standing Bottoms-up One Arm Shoulder Press.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Shoulders/Kettlebell Standing Bottoms-up One Arm Shoulder Press1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Shoulders/Kettlebell Standing Bottoms-up One Arm Shoulder Press.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
