c3b24070-4f57-4e30-ad68-acfd290dd4fc	Kettlebell sumo deadlift	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	7352a8b5-30da-44d7-9cae-8a031f5d2aed	1. Place a kettlebell on the floor between your feet. Stand with your feet wider than shoulder-width apart and your toes pointed slightly outward. \r\n2. Hinge at your hips and bend your knees to lower your body, reaching down to grasp the kettlebell handle with both hands, keeping your back straight and chest up.\r\n3. Push through your heels to lift the kettlebell off the floor, extending your hips and knees simultaneously.\r\n4. Lower the kettlebell back to the starting position. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Ensure your knees track over your toes to prevent knee strain.\r\n2. Maintain a wide stance with toes pointed slightly outward.\r\n3. Use a weight that allows you to maintain proper form throughout the exercise.	{"video_url": "videos/Back/Kettlebell Sumo Deadlift.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Back/Kettlebell Sumo Deadlift1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Back/Kettlebell Sumo Deadlift.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
