3f53a382-e124-4d2c-aff3-a0ca56ded009	Kettlebell Sumo Deadlift with High Pull	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	7352a8b5-30da-44d7-9cae-8a031f5d2aed	1. Place a kettlebell on the floor between your feet. Stand with your feet wider than shoulder-width apart and your toes pointed slightly outward. \r\n2. Hinge at your hips and bend your knees to lower your body, reaching down to grasp the kettlebell handle with both hands, keeping your back straight and chest up.\r\n3. Push through your heels to lift the kettlebell off the floor, extending your hips and knees simultaneously. As you reach the standing position, explosively pull the kettlebell upward towards your chin by bending your elbows and keeping them pointed outward.\r\n4. Lower the kettlebell back to the starting position with control. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Use a weight that allows you to maintain proper form throughout the exercise.\r\n2. Push through your heels to maximize power and stability.\r\n3. Ensure your knees track over your toes to prevent knee strain.	{"video_url": "videos/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Kettlebell Sumo Deadlift with High Pull.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Kettlebell Sumo Deadlift with High Pull1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Kettlebell Sumo Deadlift with High Pull.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
fc3cad6e-4adc-4d8b-9eba-0209beeb65cb	Kettlebell sumo squat	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	7352a8b5-30da-44d7-9cae-8a031f5d2aed	1. Stand with your feet wider than shoulder-width apart, toes pointed slightly outward. Hold a kettlebell with both hands close to your chest.\r\n2. Hinge at your hips while bending your knees to lower your body into a squat.\r\n3. Lower yourself until your thighs are parallel to the floor or slightly below.\r\n4. Push through your heels to rise back to the starting position, fully extending your hips and knees. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Ensure your knees track over your toes to prevent knee strain.\r\n2. Exhale as you rise from the squat, inhale as you lower into it.\r\n3. Maintain a wide stance with toes pointed slightly outward.	{"video_url": "videos/Legs/Kettlebell Sumo Squat.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Legs/Kettlebell Sumo Squat1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Legs/Kettlebell Sumo Squat.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
498d6c60-d809-47a2-bc0f-5ed00d3e5e04	Kettlebell sumo squat (version 2)	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	7352a8b5-30da-44d7-9cae-8a031f5d2aed	1. Stand with your feet wider than shoulder-width apart, toes pointed slightly outward. Hold a kettlebell with both hands, letting it hang down between your legs.\r\n2. Hinge at your hips while bending your knees to lower your body into a squat.\r\n3. Lower yourself until your thighs are parallel to the floor or slightly below.\r\n4. Push through your heels to rise back to the starting position, fully extending your hips and knees. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Ensure your knees track over your toes to prevent knee strain.\r\n2. Exhale as you rise from the squat, inhale as you lower into it.\r\n3. Maintain a wide stance with toes pointed slightly outward.	{"video_url": "videos/Legs/Kettlebell Sumo Squat (VERSION 2).mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Legs/Kettlebell Sumo Squat (VERSION 2)1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Legs/Kettlebell Sumo Squat (VERSION 2).jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
c08f356c-40ca-4b70-91b0-3d2094b9d10b	Kettlebell sumo squat off stepbox	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	7352a8b5-30da-44d7-9cae-8a031f5d2aed	1. Stand between two stepboxes with a wide stance, toes pointed slightly outward. Hold a kettlebell with both hands, letting it hang between your legs.\r\n2. Lower yourself into a wide squat by bending your knees and pushing your hips back. Lower until your thighs are parallel to the floor.\r\n3. Push through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top of the movement.\r\n4. Repeat the squat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Ensure your knees track over your toes and do not collapse inward during the squat.\r\n2. Keep your back straight and chest up to avoid leaning forward.\r\n3. Use a weight that challenges your strength but allows you to maintain proper form.	{"video_url": "videos/Legs/Kettlebell Sumo Squat off Stepbox.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Legs/Kettlebell Sumo Squat off Stepbox1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Legs/Kettlebell Sumo Squat off Stepbox.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
4426062b-b43e-4548-a2d4-ff7b372ac95c	Kettlebell swing	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	7352a8b5-30da-44d7-9cae-8a031f5d2aed	1. Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart, toes pointing slightly outward. Place a kettlebell on the floor between your feet. Bend at your hips and knees to reach forward and grab the kettlebell with both hands, keeping your back straight and chest up.\r\n2. Hinge at your hips to swing the kettlebell back between your legs, allowing a slight bend in your knees.\r\n3. Drive through your hips, extending them forcefully to swing the kettlebell forward and up to shoulder height. Allow the momentum to carry the kettlebell upwards, keeping your arms straight but not locked.\r\n4. As the kettlebell begins to descend, hinge at your hips again to let it swing back between your legs, preparing for the next repetition. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Use the power from your hips, not your arms, to generate the swing.\r\n2. Keep your back straight and avoid rounding your shoulders.\r\n3. Exhale as you swing the kettlebell up, inhale as it swings back down.	{"video_url": "videos/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Kettlebell Swing.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Kettlebell Swing1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Kettlebell Swing.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
fbed0068-0a99-4787-ae7d-53db1330f487	Kettlebell swing (Version 2)	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	7352a8b5-30da-44d7-9cae-8a031f5d2aed	1. Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart, toes pointing slightly outward. Place a kettlebell vertically on the floor between your feet. Bend at your hips and knees to reach forward and grab the kettlebell with both hands, interlocking your fingers.\r\n2. Hinge at your hips to swing the kettlebell back between your legs, allowing a slight bend in your knees.\r\n3. Drive through your hips, extending them forcefully to swing the kettlebell forward and up to shoulder height. Allow the momentum to carry the kettlebell upwards, keeping your arms straight but not locked.\r\n4. As the kettlebell begins to descend, hinge at your hips again to let it swing back between your legs, preparing for the next repetition. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Use the power from your hips, not your arms, to generate the swing.\r\n2. Keep your back straight and avoid rounding your shoulders.\r\n3. Exhale as you swing the kettlebell up, inhale as it swings back down.	{"video_url": "videos/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Kettlebell Swing (Version 2).mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Kettlebell Swing (Version 2)1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Kettlebell Swing (Version 2).jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
6cd69c53-979e-401b-aed8-02600b853cb6	Kettlebell thruster	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	7352a8b5-30da-44d7-9cae-8a031f5d2aed	1. Begin by standing with your feet shoulder-width apart, holding a kettlebell in each hand at shoulder level, palms facing inward. Keep your elbows close to your.\r\n2. Lower into a squat by bending your hips and knees until your thighs are parallel to the floor.\r\n3. Push through your heels to stand back up while simultaneously pressing the kettlebells overhead. Fully extend your arms at the top of the movement.\r\n4. Lower the kettlebells back to shoulder level as you prepare for the next repetition. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Exhale as you press the kettlebells overhead, inhale as you lower into the squat.\r\n2. Choose an appropriate weight to maintain control throughout the exercise.\r\n3. Keep your wrists straight and aligned with your forearms.	{"video_url": "videos/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Kettlebell Thruster.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Kettlebell Thruster1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Kettlebell Thruster.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
e21266af-88fc-466e-8a66-b3e08ea029ea	Kettlebells sumo deadlift with high pull	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	7352a8b5-30da-44d7-9cae-8a031f5d2aed	1. Place two kettlebells on the floor between your feet. Stand with your feet wider than shoulder-width apart and your toes pointed slightly outward. \r\n2. Hinge at your hips and bend your knees to lower your body, reaching down to grasp the kettlebell handles, one in each hand, keeping your back straight and chest up.\r\n3. Push through your heels to lift the kettlebells off the floor, extending your hips and knees simultaneously. As you reach the standing position, pull the kettlebells upward towards your chin by bending your elbows and keeping them pointed outward.\r\n4. Lower the kettlebells back to the starting position. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Keep your back straight and avoid rounding your shoulders.\r\n2. Exhale as you lift the kettlebell and perform the high pull, inhale as you lower it.\r\n3. Push through your heels to maximize power and stability.	{"video_url": "videos/Back/Kettlebells Sumo Deadlift with High Pull.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Back/Kettlebells Sumo Deadlift with High Pull1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Back/Kettlebells Sumo Deadlift with High Pull.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
0f8fddf6-926f-4848-bd1d-8483a4918bd6	Knee to chest stretch	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	de08e8c8-a4ec-465b-ae07-cc976f64cd81	1. Stand upright with your feet hip-width apart and your arms at your sides.\r\n2. Lift your right knee towards your chest, wrapping your hands around your knee to gently pull your knee closer to your chest.\r\n3. Hold the stretch for 15-30 seconds, feeling the stretch. Keep your left leg straight and maintain your balance.\r\n4. Release your right knee and lower your leg back to the starting position. Repeat the stretch with your left knee. Alternate sides for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Use a gentle but firm grip to avoid pulling too hard and causing strain.\r\n2. Engage your core to maintain balance and stability throughout the stretch.\r\n3. Move slowly and with control to maximize the effectiveness of the stretch and avoid any sudden movements.	{"video_url": "videos/Stretching - Mobility/knee to chest stretch  .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Stretching - Mobility/knee to chest stretch  .jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
bcf35041-791c-41e7-a84d-81a2412447ed	Kneeling hip flexor stretch	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	de08e8c8-a4ec-465b-ae07-cc976f64cd81	1. Begin in a kneeling position with your right knee on the floor and your left foot in front of you, forming a 90-degree angle with your left knee.\r\n2. Place your hands on your hips or on your left thigh for support. Engage your core and keep your back straight.\r\n3. Gently push your hips forward, feeling the stretch in your right hip flexor. Hold the stretch for 15-30 seconds.\r\n4. Return to the starting position and switch legs, performing the stretch with your left knee on the floor and your right foot in front. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Ensure your front knee is directly above your ankle to avoid putting unnecessary strain on your knee joint.\r\n2. Maintain an upright posture with your shoulders relaxed and your chest open.\r\n3. Move slowly and with control to maximize the effectiveness of the stretch and avoid any sudden movements.\r\n	{"video_url": "videos/Stretching - Mobility/kneeling hip flexor stretch  .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Stretching - Mobility/kneeling hip flexor stretch  .jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
ea51aee8-cfda-4d32-89fe-edc48a372619	Kneeling lat floor stretch	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Begin in a tabletop position on the floor with your hands directly under your shoulders and your knees under your hips.\r\n2. Extend your right arm forward on the floor, palm facing up, while keeping your left hand in place.\r\n3. Bend your left elbow to lower your chest towards the floor, feeling the stretch in your lat muscles and upper back. Keep your head relaxed and look down at the floor.\r\n4. Hold the stretch for 15-30 seconds, breathing deeply and steadily. Slowly return to the starting position and repeat on the other side by extending your left arm forward and bending your right elbow.	1. Ensure your extended arm is fully extended to get the most effective stretch in your lats and upper back.\r\n2. Perform the stretch on a comfortable surface, such as a yoga mat, to prevent discomfort or injury.\r\n3. Relax your shoulders and neck to avoid tension in these areas.	{"video_url": "videos/Stretching - Mobility/kneeling lat floor stretch.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Stretching - Mobility/kneeling lat floor stretch1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Stretching - Mobility/kneeling lat floor stretch.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
765d513e-bb9b-4a0c-87ee-a1d90a51c0d5	Kneeling leg curl machine	Resistance	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	8239c9cf-c829-4bdb-9d7d-53776a47155a	1. Kneel on the leg curl machine with one leg bent on the knee rest behind you and the other leg extended and secured under the pad.\r\n2. Hold onto the handles for stability and keep your back straight.\r\n3. Curl the extended leg by bending your knee and pulling your heel towards your glutes, squeezing your hamstrings at the top of the movement.\r\n4. Slowly return your leg to the starting position with control. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions, then switch legs.	1. Keep your back straight and avoid arching or rounding your spine.\r\n2. Focus on engaging your hamstrings throughout the movement.\r\n3. Exhale as you curl your leg up and inhale as you lower it back down.	{"video_url": "videos/Legs/kneeling leg curl machine  .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Legs/kneeling leg curl machine  .jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
429553a3-63cd-4614-9231-c31dbd43a6bd	Kneeling squat jumps bodyweight	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Begin in a kneeling position on the floor with your knees hip-width apart and your toes pointing behind you. Sit back on your heels with your arms at your sides.\r\n2. Engage your core and glutes, then swing your arms forward and upward to generate momentum.\r\n3. Explosively jump up from your knees, bringing your feet forward to land in a squat position with your feet shoulder-width apart and your knees bent.\r\n4. Stand up from the squat position and then return to the starting kneeling position. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Use your arms to generate momentum and assist with the jump.\r\n2. Land softly on your forefeet to reduce impact on your joints.\r\n3. Ensure your knees are aligned with your toes when you land in the squat position to avoid strain.	{"video_url": "videos/Legs/Kneeling Squat Jumps bodyweight  .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Legs/Kneeling Squat Jumps bodyweight  .jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
1b7ab539-a61f-4874-acfe-d26755d36ccf	Kneeling wrist flexor stretch	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	de08e8c8-a4ec-465b-ae07-cc976f64cd81	1. Begin in a tabletop position on the floor with your hands directly under your shoulders and your knees under your hips.\r\n2. Rotate your hands so that your fingers are pointing towards your knees, palms flat on the floor.\r\n3. Slowly shift your weight back towards your heels to increase the stretch in your wrists and forearms, keeping your palms flat on the floor.\r\n4. Hold the stretch for 15-30 seconds, breathing deeply and steadily. Release the stretch by shifting your weight forward and gently lifting your hands off the floor. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Keep your palms flat on the floor and your fingers pointing towards your knees to maximize the stretch in your wrist flexors.\r\n2. Move slowly and with control to avoid any sudden movements that could cause strain.\r\n3. If the stretch is too intense, reduce the angle by bringing your hands closer to your knees.	{"video_url": "videos/Stretching - Mobility/kneeling wrist flexor stretch  .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Stretching - Mobility/kneeling wrist flexor stretch  .jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
19c7a523-a570-4e74-aecc-a32be7f68585	Landmine chest press	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	68ed06e5-fd1e-4198-8eea-6b4b13e3ede2	1. Begin by standing with your feet shoulder-width apart, holding the end of a barbell with the right hand at chest level. The other end of the barbell should be anchored securely in a landmine attachment or corner.\r\n2. Press the barbell forward and slightly upward until your arm is fully extended.\r\n3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the top of the movement.\r\n4. Slowly lower the barbell back to the starting position at chest level. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Keep your back straight and avoid arching it during the press.\r\n2. Exhale as you press the barbell forward and inhale as you lower it back.\r\n3. Focus on using your chest muscles to press the barbell.	{"video_url": "videos/Chest/landmine chest  press  .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Chest/landmine chest  press.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
58ab0c2e-2e92-4006-ba46-df65ff20527c	Landmine row	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	68ed06e5-fd1e-4198-8eea-6b4b13e3ede2	1. Begin by standing with your feet shoulder-width apart and knees slightly bent. Position yourself so that the end of a barbell, anchored in a landmine attachment or a secure corner, is between your feet.\r\n2. Bend at the hips and knees to lean forward and grab the barbell with both hands using a v handle.\r\n3. Pull the barbell towards your chest by squeezing your shoulder blades together and bending your elbows.\r\n4. Lower the barbell back to the starting position with control, fully extending your arms. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Exhale as you pull the barbell towards you and inhale as you lower it back.\r\n2. Ensure your feet are firmly planted and your stance is stable.\r\n3. Focus on squeezing your shoulder blades together to engage your middle back muscles.	{"video_url": "videos/Back/Landmine row.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Back/Landmine row1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Back/Landmine row.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
