b951ae93-7048-4482-89fc-511826810923	lateral raises dumbbell seated with swing	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Sit on a bench with your feet flat on the floor, holding a dumbbell in each hand with your arms hanging by your sides and palms facing your body. Keep your torso leaning towards the floor.\r\n2. Begin raising your torso while swinging both arms out to the sides until they reach shoulder height, using a controlled momentum and bending your elbows at 90 degrees as you raise up.\r\n3. Pause briefly at the top of the movement, ensuring your arms are parallel and your torso vertical to the floor.\r\n4. Lower the dumbbells back to the starting position with control. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Do not raise the dumbbells higher than shoulder height to prevent shoulder strain.\r\n2. Use a controlled swing to lift the weights; avoid excessive momentum.\r\n3. Exhale as you lift the dumbbells and inhale as you lower them.	{"video_url": "videos/Shoulders/Lateral raises dumbbell seated with swing.mp4"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
a07be2f6-b5c8-4237-9115-ca51fe0bb259	Lateral raises on cable machine	Resistance	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Stand with your right side facing the cable machine, feet shoulder-width apart. Attach a handle to the low pulley and grasp the handle with your left hand, palm facing inward.\r\n2. Raise the handle out to your side until your left arm is parallel to the floor, keeping a slight bend in your elbow.\r\n3. Slowly lower the handle back to the starting position with control. \r\n4.Repeat for the desired number of repetitions, then switch sides to work the opposite arm.	1. Keep your back straight and avoid using momentum.\r\n2. Focus on engaging your shoulder muscles throughout the movement.\r\n3. Exhale as you raise the handle and inhale as you lower it back down.	{"video_url": "videos/Shoulders/lateral raises on cable machine.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Shoulders/lateral raises on cable machine1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Shoulders/lateral raises on cable machine.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
55048852-4b39-4d15-9b15-8cbdd9375e87	Leaning Dumbbell Lateral Raise	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	bfdb4696-9395-413b-bf0f-675c7a90d3be	1. Stand next to a lifting cage, holding a dumbbell in your right hand. Grasp the lifting cage bar for support with your left hand and lean your body to the opposite side by extending your arm.\r\n2. With your right arm hanging down, raise the dumbbell out to your side until your arm is parallel to the floor, keeping a slight bend in your elbow and your palm facing down.\r\n3. Lower the dumbbell back to the starting position with control. Complete the desired number of repetitions.	1. Avoid using momentum; lift the dumbbell with control.\r\n2. Exhale as you lift the dumbbell and inhale as you lower it.\r\n3. Maintain a slight bend in your elbow throughout the exercise.	{"video_url": "videos/Shoulders/Leaning dumbbell lateral raise.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Shoulders/Leaning dumbbell lateral raise1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Shoulders/Leaning dumbbell lateral raise.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
5c057f87-9a00-42f9-ae79-5658f82ac660	Leg extended stretch on bench	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	de08e8c8-a4ec-465b-ae07-cc976f64cd81	1. Begin by sitting on the edge of a bench with both legs bent and your feet flat on the floor. Keep your back straight and your core engaged.\r\n2. Extend your right leg forward until it is parallel to the floor, keeping your leg straight.\r\n3. Hold the stretch for 15-30 seconds, feeling the stretch in your hamstring and lower back.\r\n4. Slowly bring your right leg back to the starting position with both feet flat on the floor. Repeat the stretch with your left leg extended. Alternate sides for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Ensure your extended leg is straight and parallel to the floor to get the most effective stretch.\r\n2. Perform the stretch on a stable, non-slip surface to prevent discomfort or injury.\r\n3. If you find it difficult to hold your leg up, you can use your hands to support your thigh.	{"video_url": "videos/Stretching - Mobility/Leg extended stretch on bench.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Stretching - Mobility/Leg extended stretch on bench1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Stretching - Mobility/Leg extended stretch on bench.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
62c61eb4-36fb-4305-8f95-7cf60e95548f	Oblique crunch	Resistance	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Lie on your back with your knees bent and feet flat on the floor. Place your hands behind your head, keeping your elbows wide.\r\n2. Engage your core muscles and lift your upper back off the floor, rotating your abdomen to raise your right elbow towards the ceiling.\r\n3. Squeeze your obliques at the top of the movement and slowly lower your upper back to the starting position with control.\r\n4. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions, then switch sides to work the opposite oblique.	1. Exhale as you lift and rotate your upper body, and inhale as you lower it back down.\r\n2. Avoid pulling on your neck with your hands; let your abs do the work.\r\n3. Focus on engaging your oblique muscles throughout the movement.	{"video_url": "videos/Abdominals/oblique crunch .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Abdominals/oblique crunch.jpeg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
b4c20837-04f0-4392-b4de-91f15cde8129	Leg lift circles	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Lie on your back with your legs extended and your arms at your sides, palms facing down.\r\n2. Lift both legs off the floor, about a foot above the floor, keeping your legs straight and your core engaged.\r\n3. Begin to draw small circles in the air with both legs moving together in a controlled and steady motion. Perform the circles in one direction for a set number of repetitions.\r\n4. Switch directions and draw circles with both legs in the opposite direction for the same number of repetitions. Lower your legs back to the starting position.	1. Keep your legs as straight as possible to maximize the stretch and engagement in your hip flexors and quadriceps.\r\n2. Perform the exercise on a comfortable, non-slip surface to prevent discomfort or injury.\r\n3. If you find it difficult to keep your legs straight, you can start with smaller circles and gradually increase the size as you build strength and flexibility.	{"video_url": "videos/Abdominals/leg lift circles .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Abdominals/leg lift circles.jpeg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
0084a8e2-a194-4e36-ab96-352486209267	Leg press machine close stance	Resistance	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	28deca28-3c3f-422f-9707-032a51268ee5	1. Sit on the leg press machine and position your feet close together in the center of the foot platform, keeping your feet flat and parallel. Adjust the seat so that your knees are bent at about a 90-degree angle.\r\n2. Hold the handles on the sides of the seat for stability. Keep your back pressed against the backrest and your core engaged.\r\n3. Press through your heels to extend your legs, pushing the platform away from you until your legs are fully extended but not locked at the knees.\r\n4. Slowly return to the starting position by bending your knees with control. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Keep your back pressed against the backrest throughout the exercise.\r\n2. Ensure both feet remain flat on the platform for better stability and muscle balance.\r\n3. Exhale as you press the platform away and inhale as you return to the starting position.	{"video_url": "videos/Legs/leg press machine close stance  .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Legs/leg press machine close stance  .jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
