b032377a-d8fc-4410-81ec-e2fa09e7853b	Lunge front kick	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Stand upright with your feet hip-width apart and your arms at your sides.\r\n2. Lift your right leg to perform a front kick, extending your leg straight out in front of you.\r\n3. As you bring your right leg back down, step it behind you into a lunge position, lowering your hips until your left thigh is parallel to the floor and your right knee nearly touches the floor.\r\n4. Push through your left heel to stand back up, returning to the starting position. Repeat the movement on the same side or alternate legs for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Ensure your front knee is aligned with your ankle during the lunge to avoid strain.\r\n2. Perform the front kick with control, avoiding any jerky movements to prevent injury.\r\n3. Focus on steady breathing, exhaling as you perform the front kick and inhaling as you lower into the lunge.	{"video_url": "videos/Legs/lunge front kick  .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Legs/lunge front kick  .jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
c5f48978-ba60-41b1-a94b-bd16bd77791e	Lunge pulses bodyweight	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Stand upright with your feet hip-width apart. Step your right foot forward into a lunge position, lowering your hips until your right thigh is parallel to the floor and your left knee nearly touches the floor.\r\n2. From the lunge position, perform small pulses by slightly raising and lowering your hips in a controlled manner. \r\n3. Continue pulsing for the desired number of repetitions or duration, keeping your core engaged and maintaining balance.\r\n4. Return to the starting position by pushing through your right heel and repeat the exercise on the opposite leg.	1. Ensure your front knee is aligned with your ankle and does not extend past your toes to avoid strain.\r\n2. Use a controlled motion and avoid bouncing to maintain muscle tension and effectiveness.\r\n3. Perform the pulses with control, avoiding any jerky movements to prevent injury.	{"video_url": "videos/Legs/lunge pulses bodyweight.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Legs/lunge pulses bodyweight1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Legs/lunge pulses bodyweight.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
9bb1c7ba-642d-4a47-9a6d-6dfeb2a0f5e8	Lunge reverse with Resistance band	Resistance	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	0496ab82-eab1-4362-8dca-c3f5cd24f67f	1. Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart, placing the middle of the resistance band under your left foot. Hold the handles of the resistance band at shoulder height with your elbows bent and facing the floor.\r\n2. Step your right leg back into a reverse lunge, bending both knees to lower your right knee towards the floor while keeping your left knee aligned with your ankle.\r\n3. Push through your left heel to return to the starting position, bringing your right leg forward.\r\n4. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions, then switch sides to work the other leg.	1. Exhale as you push back up to the starting position and inhale as you lower into the lunge.\r\n2. Focus on engaging your glutes and quadriceps throughout the movement.\r\n3. Ensure your front knee does not extend past your toes to avoid joint strain.	{"video_url": "videos/Legs/lunge reverse with resistance band  .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Legs/lunge reverse with resistance band  .jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
336afd7a-097d-42c4-a1d0-134adbdd7058	Lunge rotation left and right bodyweight	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Stand upright with your feet hip-width apart and your arms bent at your sides, hands close to your torso.\r\n2. Step your right foot forward into a lunge position, lowering your hips until your right thigh is parallel to the floor and your left knee nearly touches the floor.\r\n3. Rotate your torso to the right, bringing your arms to the right side, then rotate your torso to the left, bringing your arms to the left side.\r\n4. Return your torso to the center and push through your right heel to return to the starting position. Repeat the movement on the opposite leg. Alternate sides for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Ensure your front knee is aligned with your ankle and does not extend past your toes to avoid strain.\r\n2. Keep your back straight and your chest lifted to maintain proper posture.\r\n3. Perform the rotations with control, avoiding any jerky movements to prevent injury.	{"video_url": "videos/Legs/lunge rotation left and right bodyweight.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Legs/lunge rotation left and right bodyweight1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Legs/lunge rotation left and right bodyweight.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
0419b6b2-d29d-433c-a59e-616432397dc0	Lunge to knee drive left bodyweight	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Stand upright with your feet hip-width apart and your arms at your sides.\r\n2. Step your left foot back into a lunge position, lowering your hips until your right thigh is parallel to the floor and your left knee nearly touches the floor.\r\n3. Push through your right heel to stand back up, simultaneously driving your left knee up towards your chest.\r\n4. Return your left leg to the starting position and repeat for the desired number of repetitions. Switch sides and repeat the movement with your right leg stepping back.	1. Ensure your front knee is aligned with your ankle and does not extend past your toes to avoid strain.\r\n2. Perform the knee drive with control, avoiding any jerky movements to prevent injury.\r\n3. Focus on steady breathing, exhaling as you drive your knee up and inhaling as you lower into the lunge.	{"video_url": "videos/Legs/Lunge to Knee Drive left bodyweight  .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Legs/Lunge to Knee Drive left bodyweight  .jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
