6463146c-fcb1-4be5-9808-f86f3ce612ab	lunges alternate leg with pause bodyweight	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Stand upright with your feet hip-width apart and your arms at your sides.\r\n2. Step your right foot forward into a lunge position, lowering your hips until your right thigh is parallel to the floor and your left knee nearly touches the floor. Pause for a moment in this position.\r\n3. Push through your right heel to return to the starting position, then step your left foot forward into a lunge position, lowering your hips until your left thigh is parallel to the floor and your right knee nearly touches the floor. Pause for a moment in this position.\r\n4. Push through your left heel to return to the starting position. Alternate legs for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Ensure your front knee is aligned with your ankle and does not extend past your toes to avoid strain.\r\n2. Perform each lunge with control, pausing briefly to enhance muscle engagement.\r\n3. Focus on steady breathing, exhaling as you push back to the starting position and inhaling as you step forward into the lunge.	{"video_url": "videos/Legs/lunges alternate leg with pause bodyweight  .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Legs/lunges alternate leg with pause bodyweight  .jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
0fbabbd1-7191-4b8b-a5e5-bf6be9360b19	Lunges same leg side view bodyweight	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Stand upright with your feet hip-width apart and your arms at your sides.\r\n2. Step your right foot forward into a lunge position, lowering your hips until your right thigh is parallel to the floor and your left knee nearly touches the floor. Pause for a moment in this position.\r\n3. Push through your right heel to return to the starting position.\r\n4. Repeat the lunge with your right leg for the desired number of repetitions before switching to your left leg.	1. Focus on steady breathing, exhaling as you push back to the starting position and inhaling as you step forward into the lunge.\r\n2. Keep your back straight and your chest lifted to maintain proper posture.\r\n3. Use a controlled motion when bringing your leg back to the starting position to maintain balance.	{"video_url": "videos/Legs/lunges same leg side view bodyweight.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Legs/lunges same leg side view bodyweight1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Legs/lunges same leg side view bodyweight.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
59cf8ef1-dbeb-496e-8afb-efdd7a3e8a02	Lunging straight leg calf stretch	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	de08e8c8-a4ec-465b-ae07-cc976f64cd81	1. Stand upright with your feet hip-width apart and your arms at your sides.\r\n2. Step your right foot back into a lunge position, keeping your right leg straight and your heel on the floor. Bend your left knee slightly, keeping your left foot flat on the floor.\r\n3. Lean forward slightly, pressing your hips downward and feeling the stretch in your right calf. Hold this position for 15-30 seconds.\r\n4. Return to the starting position and switch legs, stepping your left foot back and repeating the stretch.	1. Ensure your back leg remains straight and your heel stays on the floor to maximize the stretch in your calf.\r\n2. Keep your front knee aligned with your ankle to avoid unnecessary strain on your joints.\r\n3. Perform the stretch on a stable, non-slip surface to prevent slipping or discomfort.	{"video_url": "videos/Stretching - Mobility/lunging straight leg calf stretch.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Stretching - Mobility/lunging straight leg calf stretch1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Stretching - Mobility/lunging straight leg calf stretch.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
4f021ab0-a2b5-4792-957e-1717d5dfe233	lying (prone) abdominal stretch	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	de08e8c8-a4ec-465b-ae07-cc976f64cd81	1. Begin by lying face down on the floor with your legs extended straight behind you and your hands placed under your shoulders, palms flat on the floor.\r\n2. Slowly press your hands into the floor to lift your chest upward, extending your spine. Keep your hips and legs relaxed on the floor.\r\n3. Continue to lift your chest until you feel a comfortable stretch in your abdomen and lower back. Hold this position for 15-30 seconds, keeping your elbows slightly bent.\r\n4. Slowly lower your chest back down to the floor and return to the starting position. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Avoid locking your elbows; keep them slightly bent to prevent strain on your joints.\r\n2. Breathe deeply and steadily, inhaling as you lift your chest and exhaling as you hold the stretch.\r\n3. Perform the stretch on a comfortable surface, such as a yoga mat, to prevent discomfort or injury.	{"video_url": "videos/Stretching - Mobility/lying (prone) abdominal stretch.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Stretching - Mobility/lying (prone) abdominal stretch1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Stretching - Mobility/lying (prone) abdominal stretch.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
c2588efd-ce1b-48bb-bb89-b6595e122434	Lying abs Resistance band	Resistance	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	0496ab82-eab1-4362-8dca-c3f5cd24f67f	1. Lie on your back with your knees bent and feet flat on the floor. Attach the resistance band to a low anchor point behind your head and hold the handles with both hands, keeping your arms bent and handles close to your head.\r\n2. Curl your upper body, bringing your elbows towards your knees while lifting your back off the floor. \r\n3. Slowly lower your upper body back to the starting position with control. \r\n4. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Exhale as you curl your torso up and inhale as you lower it back down.\r\n2. Keep your feet flat on the floor for better stability.\r\n3. Focus on engaging your abdominal muscles throughout the movement.	{"video_url": "videos/Abdominals/lying abs resistance band .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Abdominals/lying abs resistance band.jpeg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
c795f697-004e-475a-86d1-658a59933c4d	Lying back extension	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Begin by lying face down on the floor with your legs extended straight behind you and your hands placed behind your head, elbows out to the sides.\r\n2. Engage your core and glutes, then lift your upper torso off the floor, keeping your neck in a neutral position and your lower body relaxed on the floor.\r\n3. Hold the top position for a moment, squeezing your lower back muscles.\r\n4. Slowly lower your upper torso back to the starting position with control. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Keep your neck in a neutral position to avoid straining it.\r\n2. Perform the exercise on a comfortable, non-slip surface to prevent discomfort or injury.\r\n3. If you find it challenging to lift your upper torso, you can start with smaller movements and gradually increase the range of motion as you build strength.	{"video_url": "videos/Back/lying back extension .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Back/lying back extension .jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
8609693e-8a77-4d9a-b17b-2fd5849d282b	Lying bench external shoulder rotation	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Lie on your back on a bench with your arms extended out to the sides, your elbows bent at 90 degrees, and your forearms hanging off the sides of the bench, perpendicular to the floor in line with your head.\r\n2. Rotate your shoulders to lift your forearms upward until they are vertical to the floor, maintaining the 90-degree angle at your elbows throughout the movement.\r\n3. Slowly lower your forearms back to the starting position with control. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Keep your core engaged and your back flat against the bench to maintain stability.\r\n2. Move slowly and with control to maximize muscle engagement and prevent injury.\r\n3. Keep your elbows fixed at a 90-degree angle throughout the movement to isolate the shoulder rotation.	{"video_url": "videos/Shoulders/lying bench external shoulder rotation.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Shoulders/lying bench external shoulder rotation1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Shoulders/lying bench external shoulder rotation.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
0639ed5f-f33c-4839-87ae-50d9e48118cb	Lying bench internal rotation stretch	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Lie on your back on a bench with your arms extended out to the sides, your elbows bent at 90 degrees, and your forearms hanging off the sides of the bench, perpendicular to the floor in line with your torso.\r\n2. Rotate your shoulders to lift your forearms upward until they are vertical to the floor, maintaining the 90-degree angle at your elbows throughout the movement.\r\n3. Slowly lower your forearms back to the starting position with control. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Keep your core engaged and your back flat against the bench to maintain stability.\r\n2. Move slowly and with control to maximize muscle engagement and prevent injury.\r\n3. Keep your elbows fixed at a 90-degree angle throughout the movement to isolate the shoulder rotation.	{"video_url": "videos/Shoulders/lying bench internal rotation stretch.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Shoulders/lying bench internal rotation stretch1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Shoulders/lying bench internal rotation stretch.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
821b9a2e-b2a5-4913-9846-bba6a3d572d3	Lying crossover stretch	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Lie on your back with your legs extended straight and your arms out to the sides to form a T shape.\r\n2. Bend and lift your right leg and cross it over your body, aiming to touch the floor on the left side, and extend your left arm to hold your right knee down. \r\n3. Hold the stretch for 15-30 seconds, feeling the stretch in your lower back and hips.\r\n4. Slowly return your right leg to the starting position. Repeat the stretch with your left leg, crossing it over your body to the right side. Alternate sides for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Move slowly and with control to avoid any sudden movements that could cause strain.\r\n2. Focus on deep, steady breathing, inhaling as you lift your leg and exhaling as you hold the stretch.\r\n3. Avoid forcing your leg to touch the floor if you feel any pain; go as far as your flexibility allows.	{"video_url": "videos/Stretching - Mobility/lying crossover stretch  .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Stretching - Mobility/lying crossover stretch  .jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
3095c52c-cec4-462b-b17c-1383655890dc	Lying glute stretch	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	de08e8c8-a4ec-465b-ae07-cc976f64cd81	1. Lie on your back with your knees bent and feet flat on the floor.\r\n2. Cross your right ankle over your left knee, forming a figure-four position.\r\n3. Grasp the back of your left thigh with both hands and gently pull your left leg towards your chest. Hold the stretch for 15-30 seconds, feeling the stretch in your right glute and hip.\r\n4. Slowly release your left leg and return to the starting position. Repeat the stretch with your left ankle crossed over your right knee. Alternate sides for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Keep your head and shoulders relaxed on the floor to avoid tension in your neck and upper back.\r\n2. Avoid pulling too hard; go as far as your flexibility allows without causing pain.\r\n3. Use a towel or strap if needed to assist in pulling your leg towards your chest.\r\n	{"video_url": "videos/Stretching - Mobility/lying glute stretch  .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Stretching - Mobility/lying glute stretch  .jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
582301e4-8a1d-4fab-b971-5fcf64d8577a	Lying hip flexor stretch	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	de08e8c8-a4ec-465b-ae07-cc976f64cd81	1. Lie on your back with your legs straight on the floor.\r\n2. Lift your right knee towards your chest, holding it with both hands to keep it close while extending your left leg straight off floor, keeping it in line with your right foot.\r\n3. Hold the stretch for 15-30 seconds, then slowly release your right knee and return to the starting position. Repeat the stretch with your left knee lifted towards your chest and your right leg extended. Alternate sides for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Keep your lower back pressed into the floor to avoid strain and to deepen the stretch.\r\n2. Start with a smaller range of motion if you feel any discomfort, gradually increasing as flexibility improves.\r\n3. Focus on deep, steady breathing, inhaling as you prepare for the stretch and exhaling as you hold the stretch.	{"video_url": "videos/Stretching - Mobility/lying hip flexor stretch  .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Stretching - Mobility/lying hip flexor stretch  .jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
2b81d125-4b69-4e68-b70d-2025a1249c80	Lying lateral raises bodyweight	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Lie face down on the floor with your legs extended straight and your arms extended out to your sides, palms facing down.\r\n2. Lift both arms straight upwards, keeping them in line with your shoulders. Maintain a slight bend in your elbows.\r\n3. Hold the top position for a second, feeling the contraction in your shoulder and upper back muscles.\r\n4. Slowly lower your arms back to the starting position with control. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Maintain a slight bend in your elbows to reduce strain on your joints.\r\n2. Perform the exercise on a comfortable, non-slip surface to prevent discomfort or injury.\r\n3. Move slowly and with control to maximize muscle engagement and prevent injury.	{"video_url": "videos/Shoulders/lying lateral raises bodyweight.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Shoulders/lying lateral raises bodyweight1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Shoulders/lying lateral raises bodyweight.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
276006e0-8ae5-4d06-9b31-a82fb4c11e04	Lying leg curl machine	Resistance	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Lie face down on the lying leg curl machine, positioning your legs under the padded lever, just above your ankles. Adjust the machine so that your knees are just off the edge of the bench.\r\n2. Grasp the handles on the sides of the machine for stability and keep your back flat against the bench.\r\n3. Curl your legs up towards your glutes by bending your knees, squeezing your hamstrings at the top of the movement.\r\n4. Slowly lower the padded lever back to the starting position with control, fully extending your legs. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Keep your hips pressed against the bench throughout the exercise to isolate the hamstring muscles.\r\n2. Avoid using momentum; let your muscles do the work.\r\n3. Exhale as you curl your legs up and inhale as you lower them back down.	{"video_url": "videos/Legs/lying leg curl machine  .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Legs/lying leg curl machine  .jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
04272c5c-3a22-4f05-b1d5-1b7d2e799d3b	Lying leg raise	Resistance	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Lie flat on your back with your legs extended and your arms at your sides, palms facing down firm on the floor.\r\n2. Engage your core muscles and press your lower back into the floor.\r\n3. Keeping your legs straight, lift them up towards the ceiling until they are perpendicular to the floor.\r\n4. Slowly lower your legs back to the starting position with control, stopping just before they touch the floor. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Exhale as you lift your legs up and inhale as you lower them back down.\r\n2. Keep your legs as straight as possible for maximum effectiveness.\r\n3. Focus on engaging your abdominal muscles throughout the movement.	{"video_url": "videos/Abdominals/lying leg raise.mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Abdominals/lying leg raise.jpeg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
6c39daba-98c3-4fb9-a8fa-fb908dab02e7	Lying pull over with Resistance band cable	Resistance	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	0496ab82-eab1-4362-8dca-c3f5cd24f67f	1. Attach the middle of the resistance band to a low anchor point behind you. Lie on your back on the floor, knees bent and feet flat on the floor, holding a handle in each hand with your arms extended straight above your head, palms facing forward.\r\n2. Keeping your arms straight, pull the handles over your head and towards the floor until your arms are in line with your body.\r\n3. Slowly return the handles to the starting position with control, keeping your arms straight. \r\n4. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Exhale as you pull the handles over your head and inhale as you return them to the starting position.\r\n2. Maintain a slight bend in your elbows to reduce strain on your joints.\r\n3. Focus on engaging your lats and chest muscles throughout the movement.	{"image_male_start": "images/Chest/lying pull over with resistance band cable.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
27cb987b-356b-4512-aa5a-fc056872e5f3	Lying quadriceps stretch	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	de08e8c8-a4ec-465b-ae07-cc976f64cd81	1. Lie face down on the floor with your legs extended straight and your arms resting by your sides.\r\n2. Bend your right knee and reach back with your right hand to grasp your right ankle or foot.\r\n3. Gently pull your right foot towards your glutes, feeling the stretch in your right quadriceps. Keep your hips pressed into the floor.\r\n4. Hold the stretch for 15-30 seconds, then slowly release your right foot and return to the starting position. Repeat the stretch on your left leg. Alternate sides for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Keep your hips pressed into the floor to maximize the stretch in your quadriceps and avoid straining your lower back.\r\n2. Move slowly and with control to avoid any sudden movements that could cause strain.\r\n3. If you cannot reach your foot comfortably, use a towel or strap around your ankle to assist with the stretch.	{"video_url": "videos/Stretching - Mobility/lying quadriceps stretch.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Stretching - Mobility/lying quadriceps stretch1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Stretching - Mobility/lying quadriceps stretch.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
