7cf83c17-4f2c-421e-b195-20b5f15b9475	Pull up normal grip	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	54938b47-43e8-47cd-9efc-18b4424e71e1	1. Stand beneath a pull-up bar and grasp it with an overhand grip (palms facing away from you), hands slightly wider than shoulder-width apart.\r\n2. Engage your back muscles and pull yourself up towards the bar by bending your elbows.\r\n3. Continue pulling until your chin is above the bar, focusing on contracting your back muscles.\r\n4. Lower yourself back to the starting position in a controlled manner, fully extending your arms. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Use a full range of motion, fully extending your arms at the bottom and pulling up until your chin is above the bar.\r\n2. Focus on engaging your back muscles, particularly the latissimus dorsi, to perform the pull-up effectively.\r\n3. Breathe steadily, exhaling as you pull up and inhaling as you lower yourself down.\r\n4. Avoid using momentum to swing your body; maintain a controlled movement throughout the exercise.\r\n5. Perform the exercise on a stable, secure pull-up bar to ensure safety.	{"video_url": "videos/Back/pull up normal grip .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Back/pull up normal grip .jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
