2d3dd61a-78d0-4fa2-b04e-9275051fbfd7	Push up and rotation	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Begin in a plank position with your hands placed shoulder-width apart and your feet together. Your body should form a straight line from head to heels.\r\n2. Lower your body towards the floor by bending your elbows, keeping them close to your body. Perform a push-up.\r\n3. As you push back up, shift your weight onto your left hand and rotate your torso to the right, raising your right arm towards the ceiling. Your body should form a T-shape.\r\n4. Return your right hand to the floor and lower your body into another push-up. Repeat the movement, this time rotating to the left and raising your left arm towards the ceiling. Alternate sides for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Breathe steadily, exhaling as you push up and rotate, and inhaling as you lower your body.\r\n2. Ensure your body forms a straight line during the push-up and rotation, avoiding any sagging or arching of the back.\r\n3. Keep your feet hip-width apart to provide a stable base for the rotation.	{"image_male_end": "images/Chest/push up and rotation1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Chest/push up and rotation.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
d1a3fcf5-d035-4da5-89a6-d5a9833481e1	Push up plus	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Begin in a plank position with your hands placed slightly wider than shoulder-width apart and your feet hip-width apart. Your body should form a straight line from head to heels.\r\n2. Push through your hands to protract your shoulder blades, rounding your upper back slightly.\r\n3. Lower your body towards the floor by bending your elbows, keeping them close to your body to perform a push-up.\r\n4. Return to the plank position. Repeat the sequence for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Maintain a straight body line during the push-up, avoiding any sagging or arching of the back.\r\n2. Keep your elbows close to your body during the push-up to effectively target your chest and triceps.\r\n3. Perform the exercise on a stable, non-slip surface to prevent slipping and ensure safety.	{"video_url": "videos/Chest/Push up plus.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Chest/Push up plus1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Chest/Push up plus.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
