81e473eb-2973-48a6-bd8d-fa130b0b8107	Reaching up shoulder stretch	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	de08e8c8-a4ec-465b-ae07-cc976f64cd81	1. Stand upright with your feet shoulder-width apart.\r\n2. Bend your right elbow and bring your right arm behind your back, raising your hand upward with your palm facing out.\r\n3. Hold the stretch for 15-30 seconds, then slowly release and return to the starting position. Repeat on the other side by bending your left elbow and using your right hand to assist with the stretch.	1. Move slowly and with control to avoid any sudden movements that could cause strain.\r\n2. Keep your core engaged to maintain balance and support your lower back.\r\n3. Avoid arching your back; keep your spine neutral to maximize the stretch and prevent injury.	{"video_url": "videos/Shoulders/reaching up shoulder stretch .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Shoulders/reaching up shoulder stretch .jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
