83a7e341-9d58-4621-af2a-a2ba21f31a96	Shadow boxing	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart, one foot slightly in front of the other, and your knees slightly bent. Position your hands in front of your face in a guard position, with your elbows close to your body.\r\nBegin throwing punches in the air, alternating between jabs, crosses, hooks, and uppercuts. Use a full range of motion and rotate your hips and shoulders to generate power.\r\nMove around as you throw your punches, incorporating footwork to simulate a real boxing match. Step forward, backward, and side to side, keeping light on your feet.\r\nContinue shadow boxing for the desired duration, maintaining a steady pace and controlled movements.	1. Focus on proper form and technique with each punch to maximize effectiveness and prevent injury.\r\n2. Breathe steadily, exhaling with each punch and inhaling between movements.\r\n3. Keep your hands up in the guard position to protect your face, even while moving and throwing punches.\r\n4. Use your lower body to generate power, rotating your hips and pivoting on your feet with each punch.\r\n5. Maintain a light and agile stance, allowing you to move quickly and fluidly.	{"video_url": "videos/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Shadow Boxing  .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Calisthenics-Cardio-Functional/Shadow Boxing  .jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
