4a697a56-68ed-4e42-8fef-671b4d96690b	Upright row cable Resistance band	Resistance	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	0496ab82-eab1-4362-8dca-c3f5cd24f67f	1. Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart in the middle of a resistance band, holding a handle in each hand with an overhand grip (palms facing back). Ensure the band is taut when your arms are extended downwards.\r\n2. Lift the handles straight up towards your chin, leading with your elbows and keeping the band close to your body.\r\n3. Raise the handles until your elbows are slightly higher than your shoulders and pointing to your sides.\r\n4. Slowly lower the handles back to the starting position with control. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Breathe steadily: exhale as you lift the handles and inhale as you lower them.\r\n2. Use a resistance band that allows you to maintain control and proper form throughout the exercise.\r\n3. Avoid lifting the handles too high, which can put unnecessary strain on your shoulder joints.	{"video_url": "videos/Shoulders/upright row cable resistance band .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Shoulders/upright row cable resistance band .jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
ccdc1401-44fe-4e7d-a4f3-057ecb38470f	Upright row dumbbell	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	bfdb4696-9395-413b-bf0f-675c7a90d3be	1. Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart, holding a dumbbell in each hand with an overhand grip (palms facing your thighs). Let the dumbbells rest against your thighs.\r\n2. Lift the dumbbells straight up towards your chin, leading with your elbows and keeping the weights close to your body.\r\n3. Raise the dumbbells until your elbows are level with your shoulders, ensuring your upper arms are parallel to the floor.\r\n4. Slowly lower the dumbbells back to the starting position with control. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Breathe steadily: exhale as you lift the dumbbells and inhale as you lower them.\r\n2. Focus on using your shoulders and upper back to lift the dumbbells, avoiding excessive use of your biceps.\r\n3. Avoid lifting the dumbbells too high, which can put unnecessary strain on your shoulder joints.	{"video_url": "videos/Shoulders/upright row dumbbell.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Shoulders/upright row dumbbell1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Shoulders/upright row dumbbell.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
0123e32b-dfc3-4337-9d9e-d17538d7f17a	Upright row ez bar	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	0e9c1392-3e8d-454d-be69-641c3a69f2b9	1. Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart, holding an EZ Bar with an overhand grip (palms facing down), hands placed shoulder-width apart. Allow the barbell to rest against your thighs with your arms fully extended.\r\n2. Pull the EZ Bar upward along the front of your body by bending your elbows and lifting your upper arms.\r\n3. Continue lifting the EZ Bar until it reaches chest height, keeping your elbows higher than your wrists throughout the movement.\r\n4. Slowly lower the EZ Bar back to the starting position by extending your arms fully. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Lead with your elbows to ensure proper muscle engagement and avoid wrist strain.\r\n2. Breathe steadily, exhaling as you lift the barbell and inhaling as you lower it back down.\r\n3. Avoid using momentum or swinging your body to lift the EZ Bar.	{"video_url": "videos/Shoulders/upright row ez bar .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Shoulders/upright row ez bar .jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
a2d92b50-d25f-409c-ae18-d1ea2a4cd619	Upward rotation Bent arms	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart, arms bent at 90 degrees with your upper arms parallel to the floor, and your forearms pointing down to the floor.\r\n2. Rotate your forearms upwards until your fingers point towards the ceiling, keeping your upper arms stationary.\r\n3. Slowly rotate them back to the starting position.\r\n4. Repeat for the desired repetitions	1. Focus on using your shoulder muscles to rotate your arms, avoiding excessive use of your neck or back.\r\n2. Keep your upper arms stationary throughout the movement to ensure proper form.\r\n3. Lift your arms as high as comfortable, to avoid unnecessary strain on your shoulder joints.	{"video_url": "videos/Shoulders/upward rotation bent arms.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Shoulders/upward rotation bent arms1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Shoulders/upward rotation bent arms.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
ecc664ba-7c26-4b35-a54d-5e11940f71ca	V bar lat pull down	Resistance	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	d8a6a67e-71db-4542-9dd7-a185a3e773af	1. Sit at a lat pulldown machine with your feet flat on the floor and knees secured under the pads. Grasp the V-bar attached to the machine, arms fully extended above you, and hands shoulder-width apart.\r\n2. Pull the bar down towards your upper chest and bring your elbows downwards.\r\n3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the bottom of the movement.\r\n4. Slowly return the V-bar to the starting position. Repeat for the desired repetitions.	1. Breathe steadily: exhale as you pull the bar down and inhale as you return to the starting position.\r\n2. Focus on using your back muscles to pull the bar, avoiding excessive use of your arms.\r\n3. Keep your wrists straight and avoid bending them during the pull to prevent strain.	{"video_url": "videos/Back/v bar lat pull down .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Back/v bar lat pull down .jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
18ca941c-1eea-4d8f-a1be-8cd705ad6947	V crunches	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Lie flat on your back on the floor with your legs extended and your arms extended on the floor overhead.\r\n2. Simultaneously lift your legs and torso off the floor, reaching your hands towards your feet to form a 'V' shape with your body.\r\n3. Squeeze your abdominal muscles at the top of the movement, ensuring your hands reach towards your feet.\r\n4. Slowly lower your legs and torso back to the starting position with control. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Breathe steadily: exhale as you lift into the 'V' position and inhale as you lower back down.\r\n2. Avoid using momentum to lift your legs and torso; focus on using your abdominal muscles.\r\n3. Keep your legs and arms straight throughout the movement for maximum effectiveness.	{"video_url": "videos/Abdominals/V crunches.mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Abdominals/V crunches.jpeg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
16a4c1b1-6f1a-40e9-bdfd-29af66da0380	V up	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Lie flat on your back on the floor with your legs and arms extended so that your body forms a straight line.\r\n2. Simultaneously lift your legs and torso off the floor, reaching your hands towards your feet to form a 'V' shape with your body.\r\n3. Squeeze your abdominal muscles at the top of the movement, ensuring your hands reach towards your feet.\r\n4. Slowly lower your legs and torso back to the starting position with control. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Breathe steadily: exhale as you lift into the 'V' position and inhale as you lower back down.\r\n2. Avoid using momentum to lift your legs and torso; focus on using your abdominal muscles.\r\n3. Keep your legs and arms straight throughout the movement for maximum effectiveness.	{"video_url": "videos/Abdominals/v up .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Abdominals/v up.jpeg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
589bd45e-ea00-448f-9817-0220eb863d40	Walkout	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Stand upright with your feet shoulder-width apart and arms relaxed by your sides.\r\n2. Bend your hips and knees to place your hands on the floor before you.\r\n3. Walk your hands forward, keeping your legs straight, until you are in a plank position with your hands under your shoulders and your body forming a straight line from head to heels.\r\n4. Walk your hands back towards your feet, lifting your hips and forming an inverted V shape with your body. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Avoid letting your hips sag or rise too high when in the plank position.\r\n2. Keep your legs as straight as possible while walking your hands to and from the plank position.\r\n3. Use a mat to provide cushioning for your hands and prevent slipping.	{"video_url": "videos/Abdominals/walkout .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Abdominals/walkout.jpeg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
2955404a-c712-456c-8706-b4d59a2343c8	Wall sit bodyweight	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Stand with your back against a wall and your feet shoulder-width apart, about 2 feet away from the wall.\r\n2. Slide your back down the wall until your thighs are parallel to the floor, and your knees are directly above your ankles.\r\n3. Hold this position, keeping your back flat against the wall and your hands relaxed by your sides or on your thighs.\r\n4. Maintain the position for the desired duration, then slowly stand back up.	1. Ensure your knees do not extend past your toes to avoid placing unnecessary strain on your joints.\r\n2. Breathe steadily and avoid holding your breath during the exercise.\r\n3. Press your lower back firmly against the wall to ensure proper alignment.	{"video_url": "videos/Legs/wall sit bodyweight.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Legs/wall sit bodyweight1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Legs/wall sit bodyweight.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
19c10f33-cbde-4d8e-9951-62e328e45dca	Wall squat bodyweight	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Stand with your back against a wall and your feet shoulder-width apart, about 2 feet away from the wall.\r\n2. Slide your back down the wall until your thighs are parallel to the floor and your knees are at a 90-degree angle, ensuring your knees are directly above your ankles.\r\n3. Push through your heels to stand back up, sliding your back up the wall until you return to the starting position.\r\n4. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Ensure your knees do not extend past your toes to avoid placing unnecessary strain on your joints.\r\n2. Breathe steadily: inhale as you lower into the squat and exhale as you stand back up.\r\n3. Press your lower back firmly against the wall to ensure proper alignment and support.	{"video_url": "videos/Legs/wall squat bodyweight.mp4", "image_male_end": "images/Legs/wall squat bodyweight1.jpg", "image_male_start": "images/Legs/wall squat bodyweight.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
7d8b8274-7a8d-4c73-bd20-40085047b19a	Wall squat with pause bodyweight	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Stand with your back against a wall and your feet shoulder-width apart, about 2 feet away from the wall.\r\n2. Slide your back down the wall until your thighs are parallel to the floor and your knees are at a 90-degree angle, ensuring your knees are directly above your ankles.\r\n3. Pause for 5-10 seconds and then push through your heels to stand back up, sliding your back up the wall until you return to the starting position.\r\n4. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Ensure your knees do not extend past your toes to avoid placing unnecessary strain on your joints.\r\n2. Breathe steadily: inhale as you lower into the squat and exhale as you stand back up.\r\n3. Press your lower back firmly against the wall to ensure proper alignment and support.	{"video_url": "videos/Legs/wall squat with pause bodyweight  .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Legs/wall squat with pause bodyweight  .jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
addd93dd-1fd3-4cdc-9991-9399c92362c3	weighted standing shoulder press with plate	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	ba1cac69-c4db-4c14-8076-0f34af9c1f91	1. Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart, holding a weight plate with both hands at chest level, elbows bent and pointing down.\r\n2. Press the plate upward by extending your arms fully above your head, keeping your core tight and your back straight.\r\n3. Lower the plate back down to chest level in a controlled manner.\r\n4. Repeat the movement for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Breathe steadily: exhale as you press the plate up and inhale as you lower it down.\r\n2. Avoid locking your elbows at the top of the press to keep tension on your shoulder muscles.\r\n3. Maintain a slight bend in your knees for better balance and support.	{"video_url": "videos/Shoulders/weighted standing shoulder press with plate .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Shoulders/weighted standing shoulder press with plate .jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
effe1235-96e9-48d0-87f5-14e3dd86a519	Wheels To Heaven	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	9ffbc39a-4891-4f46-b1f7-17bd2c6b7261	1. Lie on your back with your legs straight together, and your arms resting by your sides. Position an ab roller between your heels.\r\n2. Lift your legs up towards the ceiling, keeping them slightly bent, holding the ab roller securely between your heels.\r\n3. Engage your core and push your legs upward, raising your hips high off the floor.\r\n4. Lower your hips back down slowly keeping your legs up. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Start with a smaller range of motion if you are new to the exercise and gradually increase it as you gain strength.\r\n2. Breathe steadily: exhale as you lift your legs and hips, and inhale as you lower them back down.\r\n3. Avoid using momentum to lift your hips; focus on using your abdominal muscles.	{"video_url": "videos/Abdominals/Wheels To Heaven.mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Abdominals/Wheels To Heaven_Female.jpeg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
2a4c4d66-e201-407d-8f0d-3f3f9d8e3899	Wheels To Toes	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	9ffbc39a-4891-4f46-b1f7-17bd2c6b7261	1. Lie on your back with your legs straight together and your arms extended diagonally overhead, holding an ab roller.\r\n2. Lift your legs up towards the ceiling, keeping them straight, and simultaneously raise the ab roller towards your toes, lifting your upper back off the floor.\r\n3. Slowly lower your legs and the ab roller back down to the starting position, stopping just before they touch the floor.\r\n4. Repeat the movement for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Use a mat or soft surface to support your back and prevent discomfort.\r\n2. Ensure your lower back stays in contact with the floor when your legs are lowered.\r\n3. Start with a smaller range of motion if you are new to the exercise and gradually increase it as you gain strength.	{"video_url": "videos/Abdominals/Wheels To Toes.mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Abdominals/Wheels To Toes_Female.jpeg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
a3d413e5-64d7-4007-baab-1daff57f2fda	Wide push ups bodyweight	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Begin in a plank position with your hands placed wider than shoulder-width apart and your feet together. Your body should form a straight line from head to heels.\r\n2. Engage your chest and lower your body towards the floor by bending your elbows, keeping them at a 90-degree angle to your body.\r\n3. Lower your chest until it is just above the floor.\r\n4. Push through your hands to raise your body back to the starting position, fully extending your arms. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Keep your elbows at a 90-degree angle to your body to maximize chest and triceps engagement and reduce shoulder strain.\r\n2. Breathe steadily, exhaling as you push up and inhaling as you lower yourself.\r\n3. Keep your head aligned with your spine to avoid straining your neck.	{"image_male_start": "images/Chest/wide push ups bodyweight.jpg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
64ab61a8-87e9-4a94-bbc1-328d633c38fe	Wind wipers	Bodyweight	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	c262cf7f-b27f-4dc4-b751-e52a5389258b	1. Lie on your back with your arms extended out to the sides for stability, lift your legs up towards the ceiling, and keep them bent at 90 degrees.\r\n2. Lower your knees to the right side, keeping them bent together until they are just above the floor.\r\n3. Raise your knees back to the center position, and then lower them to the left side until they are just above the floor.\r\n4. Repeat the movement, alternating sides, for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Use a mat or soft surface to support your back and prevent discomfort.\r\n2. Avoid using momentum to move your legs; focus on using your abdominal and oblique muscles.\r\n3. Keep your shoulders flat on the floor to maintain stability and proper form.	{"video_url": "videos/Abdominals/wind wipers .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Abdominals/wind wipers.jpeg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
52c38816-8cb9-44f6-a100-33944ff2ef37	Wrist curl barbell	Free Weights	strength	weight_reps	intermediate	68ed06e5-fd1e-4198-8eea-6b4b13e3ede2	1. Kneel on the floor in front of a bench, placing both forearms over the bench while holding a barbell with an underhand grip (palms facing up).\r\n2. Rest your wrists just off the edge of the bench, allowing the barbell to hang downward.\r\n3. Curl the barbell upward by flexing your wrists, lifting it as high as possible while keeping your forearms flat on the bench.\r\n4. Slowly lower the barbell back to the starting position, fully extending your wrists. Repeat for the desired number of repetitions.	1. Keep your forearms pressed firmly against the bench to isolate the wrist movement.\r\n2. Use a controlled motion to lift and lower the barbell, avoiding any jerking movements.\r\n3. Avoid using your shoulder or upper arm to lift the weight.	{"video_url": "videos/Forearms/wrist curl barbell  .mp4", "image_male_start": "images/Forearms/wrist curl barbell.jpeg"}	500	t	exercise_animatic	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00	2026-08-07 07:44:48.007085+00
